{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted","id":1319165,"title":"Trying to get a sense of scale with exalted.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-17T18:00:23-07:00","id":1319165,"title":"Trying to get a sense of scale with exalted.","content":"So while there are many charms that explain part of what a character does and how insane and impressive it is, the difficulty scale only really goes up to 5 in terms of descriptions, and many exalted in their specialty *vastly* exceed that, so... what the hell does 21 successes *mean?* What can that do? Hear the shifting of tectonic plates? Leap 10 stories? In combat it's fairly well explained, but for some of the others it's harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T18:30:40-07:00","id":1319167,"title":"","content":"I think its better to ask where you are applying those 21 sux. That number is only imperative as the action its trying to accomplish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T18:37:35-07:00","id":1319168,"title":"","content":"Beyond 5, it's often &quot;Narrative fiat, within plausible (for what plausible matters with 21 freaking successes) grounds&quot;. Leaping 10 stories is the territory of Charms, I doubt any number of successes will let you do that, BUT, the jump could be incredibly successful, getting to the first or second story and granting you a large circumstantial bonus to the next roll or avoiding penalties that would have happened otherwise. If you wanna go weirder, you could make the story's progression or events go more in favor of the person who got that ungodly amount of successes (the guards show up late, there's a conveniently open window they can infiltrate instead of climbing the rest of the building, etc). It's an informal fiat way to go about it but I guess it's better than treating 21 successes the same as 5 successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T08:15:55-07:00","id":1319282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted#post1319165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what the hell does 21 successes *mean?*</div> </div> </div> </div>That you rolled a dice pool in which the odds of getting less than five successes was phenomenally low.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T08:39:18-07:00","id":1319289,"title":"","content":"Borrowing from another game, the 21 successes mean nothing, unless you make them mean something. Just rolling good doesn't mean anything unless you force yourself to need to roll that good.<br /> In other words, you have set your difficulty at 5 successes, taken all penalties into account (which you can even make up for yourself if you want), and rolled. You beat your task difficulty and succeed. Unless your task was something that counts up successes for the result, all the extra successes are just that, extra. That is the result of a succeed/fail test. You might get a cool description out of it, but really all you needed was 5 successes, and you got the number you needed plus some extra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T08:50:06-07:00","id":1319295,"title":"","content":"High successes can accomplish something truly unlikely, but the feat must still be physically possible. Something like leaping 10 stories will require Charms.<br /> <br /> The scaling of what you can accomplish tends to plateau around 10, which would represent a deed impressive enough that it could be the single greatest accomplishment of a mortal spoken of in legends (but still only a mortal).<br /> <br /> Beyond 10, it's really more about overcoming supernatural obstacles or outperforming your fellow Exalts.<br /> <br /> If you get more than 10 successes on a mundane task, then it can be represented with added style and finesse as opposed to raw strength. If 10 successes would let you lift a boulder, then 20 successes would not let you lift 2 boulders, but it might let you lift that one boulder with 1 hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T11:07:39-07:00","id":1319326,"title":"","content":"So to answer this I'm going to present how I ended mastering the game considering the difficulty system and what problems I faced, and what decisions I chosed to make to solve them.<br /> <br /> First of all, I downgraded all Stunts by 2 dices, making Stunt level 1 non existent. Most of my players describe what they do in a satisfactory way, so I don't feel the need to reward they description for &quot;baseline&quot; description, and doing a level 2 or 3 Stunt still gives you a meaningful impact mechanically (and obviously a fun time listening to the description). I did it considering the following elements :<br /> - Level 1 Stunt really slows down the game for me, because I was not use to award it, and the players waiting or asking if he has the stunt, or the forgetting of the stunt retroactively added, etc ... just for what is considered &quot;standard description&quot; what a huge hassle to me, and break the flow of my thoughts as a ST or the concentration of the players that already have a lot to take into account.<br /> <br /> - It's really easy to adjustate because you basically just need to move most of the difficulty scale accordingly, and discuss with your players solutions for special cases (difficulty 1 roll for example), but it's generally not that hard. I consider the time saved during the game by doing it way more valuable and better use (in other descriptions, RP, etc ...) that the time lost by my precedent point.<br /> <br /> - It allows to reduce the quantity of dice rolled by a little margin, and the difficulty faced by a little margin, which I appreciate as well. I don't have a problem rolling a lot of dices (it's Exalted after all), but I consider this sort of little dice trick annoying when they are supposed to happen at every roll, but are actually only awarded by conscious effort of the ST.<br /> <br /> <br /> Following this, many thoughts and problems I encountered with the difficulty system :<br /> <br /> - I believe some descriptions of difficulty were confusing to players, or at least to some of them, and induced bias of establishing the scale of difficulty between different players (ST included). Less problematic description example I think would be : stealing a gem inside a nest of serpents without being bitten. It gives enough context (serpents are implicitly normal serpents, the gem has no unusual properties, and there is enough to care about with the given description that you don't have to wonder too much about the rest of the context). But other examples were more confusing, not only to me but also to other players I had the opportunity to discuss with. For example : removing the patient appendix without killing him. I must mention that I am French (now you can read all my posts with a lovingly cute French accent), so I may not be aware about a special English-speaking expression, but to me this means a really invasive chirurgical operation with many complications possible, and that only few people in the world are able to do without mistake. Seeing this as a difficulty 1 roll, the lowest difficulty possible, did really not help me to figure out a coherent difficulty scale. Lockpicking as another example for difficulty 1, was not as problematic but still proved confusing to different players : To me it's clear it means lockpicking some random chest (the leader of a small village guarding his secrets for example), but it's totally obvious to me that the chest to an important palace in a big city is rather a difficulty 3, and I wouldn't mind making a difficulty 4-5 if the owner of the Palace was any kind of Exalted or had contacts among the Realm or Ressources, whereas to other players it would obviously be a difficulty 2, or at best 3, because it's a difficulty 1 action (lockpicking) with 1 added keyword (of quality). I believe this kind of confusion appears because contrary to the other examples of the snakes, there is a lot more room for interpretation, so different players will obviously interpret the descriptions differently.<br /> <br /> - The difficulties caping at 5 were also confusing. Especially since some of them are magical in nature, and so I didn't expect even the best mortals to be able to confront them without a good load of luck, but the system says the contrary. (Ex : Silent Wind of Hell, that I expect to find, well in the dangerous placed of Hell difficulty 4). This leads to Exalted confronting a Creation that, in it's &quot;natural phenomenas&quot;, are not really challenging. Since there is absolutely no rules or guidelines whatsoever for how to conceive harder challenges during a non-Fight type of situation, and that there is no intent explained for these design choices, I had a hard time figuring out how to appropriate those rules.<br /> <br /> All this to finally explain how I personally handle the &quot;scale&quot; of the difficulties :<br /> <br /> - Anything that I expect a human would be able to do, I put between 1 and 5.<br /> <br /> - Anything I wouldn't expect a human to do, I put between 6 and 10. In this category I also place everything that could be created by a somewhat powerful entity, that I don't think a human should be able to pass when it's not narratively important than a human passes it. For example navigating the flaming jungles in the wake of Saa'n, the Volcano God who settled its Eternal Arena of Glory inside the volcano that he set upon the Titanesque Turtle of Magma Guulmesh, set difficulties of Survival for about 7. Following the regular system, I think one would expect to put it at difficulty 4 or 5 at best (navigating a jungle in flame seems about what a human could do), but considering these flames are created by the workings of an Ancient Solar who decided to bestow himself Immortal Glory in Eternal Battle, I'm fine making them harder in context of who created them, and not only what they are.<br /> <br /> Finally, anything that is beyond 10 (with some exceptions I guess most non-confrontational tasks are at best difficulty 10), everything is a matter of confrontation. Tracking someone is your survival against their survival, and if it's 18 vs 19, well it's totally crazy, but it doesn't break creation apart my sheer power. If your players want to do lots of successes, let them waste their Essences : It's what they call &quot;Essence Fever&quot; after all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The difficulty to me what to find a good balance between number of rolls and quality of description of challenges. A simple example would be : For example : Climb a mountain. Maybe because it's not narratively important, you might just say &quot;Yeah it's difficulty 3 extended roll terminus 5 and you must gather 20 successes&quot;, the guy roll 23 successes and it's over in a over the top description. Or he takes 2-3 rolls, and you have the opportunity to ask for some cool descriptions as well &quot;After a long climb for the first hundred meters, you got to dodge some Wyld cows that are eating there&quot; and the player ask &quot;Hey I have a bit of Survival/Ride may I ride one of them to go a bit faster ?&quot; and you say &quot;Hey neat trick here is your Stunt level 2 get one WP and only 1 success bonus because remember I don't use the usual Stunt System because it makes the system simpler amInotrightlads ?&quot; and there he goes. Or maybe it's an important mountain and you got something prepared here (the exact same size than the other, but it has few narratives interests), and so you say &quot;Do me a difficulty 6 Athletics&quot; - &quot;26 wow I love this game&quot; - &quot; Well you happen to find traces that might lead to a secret temple, and ...&quot;<br /> <br /> Here were my long 50 cents, I hope it could help at least somebody.<br /> <br /> Little edit because I realised the response to the original poster was not clear : Non-confronting 11+ successes do the job, with style if you want, but does not give more, except in situations in which it would be boring to not overdo the job in description (which I believe is kinda rare). In confronting non-combat situation, well it's fun descriptions and mainly forget the scale for 11+, let them do fun while it does not break the limitations set by the rules (you can't solve the murder of Ra-Zoah the Wise because you rolled 24 successes on survival to escape the 12 successes of the Wyld Hunt tracking you)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 06-18-2019, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T11:34:33-07:00","id":1319329,"title":"","content":"I think a nice part of Storypath is that when you have these monumental success totals you can put them towards future actions in a direct mechanical fashion instead of just as a ST adjudicated bonus.<br /> <br /> I don't have a handy example for something you could do with all those extra successes on jumping high, other than stringing along a rope or some other tangentially related activity ( the example in the Storypath books is something to the effect of snipping the barbed wire when you successfully scale the fence to make it easier for your group).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T16:46:18-07:00","id":1319381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1319282#post1319282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That you rolled a dice pool in which the odds of getting less than five successes was phenomenally low.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this.<br /> <br /> Incredible things past difficulty 5 are the purview of charms, like how Unsurpassed Sight Discipline can let you spot a field mouse from a mile away. The only system that I think the game has for going past difficulty 5 is the Feats of Strength system, and even that is capped by your actual strength value, which past 5 can really only be raised by charms that specifically do that.<br /> <br /> Otherwise those giant dicepools only exist so that you can reliably do difficulty 5 tasks while in the worst conditions, or in cases where you make opposed rolls, like combat.<br /> <br /> It's somewhat less obvious for Solars, because their charms usually <i>are </i>direct continuations from what you might expect a difficulty 5 task to be. Like how the first Linguistics charm, Whirling Brush Method, can let a Solar with an ink brush record conversations as fast as a professional stenographer. It's much more obvious with Dragonblooded, who's first linguistics charm lets them whisper a phrase into the wind and deliver it miles away. Funnily enough, both of those things are likewise impossible with mere buckets of dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T02:14:50-07:00","id":1319423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1319381#post1319381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much this.<br /> <br /> Incredible things past difficulty 5 are the purview of charms, like how Unsurpassed Sight Discipline can let you spot a field mouse from a mile away. The only system that I think the game has for going past difficulty 5 is the Feats of Strength system, and even that is capped by your actual strength value, which past 5 can really only be raised by charms that specifically do that.<br /> <br /> Otherwise those giant dicepools only exist so that you can reliably do difficulty 5 tasks while in the worst conditions, or in cases where you make opposed rolls, like combat.<br /> <br /> It's somewhat less obvious for Solars, because their charms usually <i>are </i>direct continuations from what you might expect a difficulty 5 task to be. Like how the first Linguistics charm, Whirling Brush Method, can let a Solar with an ink brush record conversations as fast as a professional stenographer. It's much more obvious with Dragonblooded, who's first linguistics charm lets them whisper a phrase into the wind and deliver it miles away. Funnily enough, both of those things are likewise impossible with mere buckets of dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d add it can make extended rolls more trivial, since even at difficulty 5 ranking up the needed successes can be tricky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T05:52:20-07:00","id":1319443,"title":"","content":"Or 21 successes in performance probably means you have the ear of everyone who can hear your voice. If we want to go to more social based rolls. It means, barring charms for unnatural mental influence, that you are extraordinarily persuasive.<br /> <br /> Heck, if it were a prayer roll to the Unconquered Sun, that might be enough successes for him to raise his eyebrow at you while he looks away from his games for maybe 30 seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-20T05:35:05-07:00","id":1319677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1319443#post1319443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heck, if it were a prayer roll to the Unconquered Sun, that might be enough successes for him to raise his eyebrow at you while he looks away from his games for maybe 30 seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, guys, let\u00b4s not get crazy here<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-20T06:00:01-07:00","id":1319684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1319443#post1319443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or 21 successes in performance probably means you have the ear of everyone who can hear your voice. If we want to go to more social based rolls. It means, barring charms for unnatural mental influence, that you are extraordinarily persuasive.<br /> <br /> Heck, if it were a prayer roll to the Unconquered Sun, that might be enough successes for him to raise his eyebrow at you while he looks away from his games for maybe 30 seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was actually what happened in a short campaign I did. Some asshole decided to cheat on an Eclipse contract to let us go with their slaves in exchange of an end for the civil war. The land was destroyed by solar vengeance, and ashes rained from the skies for multiple month. After an epic quest to assemble components to make a ritual of veneration for the sun, and beg him to let us live from the earth that was damned by the malevolence of our ennemies, and a huge roll of performance, the sky opened again and dissipated the cloud of ashes. Was fun","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T04:24:39-07:00","id":1319901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted#post1319165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while there are many charms that explain part of what a character does and how insane and impressive it is, the difficulty scale only really goes up to 5 in terms of descriptions, and many exalted in their specialty *vastly* exceed that, so... what the hell does 21 successes *mean?* What can that do? Hear the shifting of tectonic plates? Leap 10 stories? In combat it's fairly well explained, but for some of the others it's harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>You either succeed or you don't. Aside from extended rolls (let's include combat in that), bonus successes don't do anything.As DrLoveMonkey says, it's so you can succeed the hardest tasks in the most difficult circumstances reliably. I'd go one further and just let the player spend the motes and succeed without rolling most of the time.<br /> <br /> If you're trying to pick a lock, you either open the lock or you don't. A normal lock made by an average locksmith might be difficulty 1, while a magic lock created by a demi-god from a bygone age might be difficulty 5. Without a very good reason, I wouldn't put a Difficulty above 5 -- if it can't be done with five successes then it can't be done (without using magic).<br /> <br /> Conceptually, leaping ten stories or hearing tectonic plates move might be difficulty 20, but I straight up wouldn't allow a roll unless you had some kind of magic (not an Excellency) to facilitate it. And if you do have such magic, chances are the difficulty is going to be lower.<br /> <br /> 21 successes should be ridiculous overkill. (Or massive unprecidented progress on an extended roll.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T08:58:57-07:00","id":1319946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted#post1319165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while there are many charms that explain part of what a character does and how insane and impressive it is, the difficulty scale only really goes up to 5 in terms of descriptions, and many exalted in their specialty *vastly* exceed that, so... what the hell does 21 successes *mean?* What can that do? Hear the shifting of tectonic plates? Leap 10 stories? In combat it's fairly well explained, but for some of the others it's harder.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you're playing 2.5 and doing social combat, then for every 3 successes above the target's mdv the target has to pay an additional willpower to resist. So if the target has an mdv of 7, then that is 4 willpower that the target has to spend to resist if it is natural mental influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T12:45:29-07:00","id":1319993,"title":"","content":"We're playing 3e, if that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T00:02:12-07:00","id":1320063,"title":"","content":"I've told my players that 5 successes constitutes a &quot;legendary success&quot;. Once one player got 10 successes on a performance (sword dance) roll, the entire assembly of Fajad (Merchants, Scholars, Nobles, Poets, Artisans, Courtesans, etc) were tripping over themselves to give him gifts and tokens of appreciation. Every palace guard, to a man, presented their sword to him and he gained the Sobriquet: Sword Dancer merit for free. Every important person in Fajad heard about his grace, and the poets were all in a race to write <i>the</i> poem about his beauty and what it meant to them. When in Fajad, he has nigh limitless access to anything he wants as everyone is bending over backwards to appease the beautiful, once in a century Flawless Master. <br /> <br /> That's 10 successes. after that, it ceases to be meaningful to mortals. 21 successes is enough to make the heavens cry, to convince the rains to fall upward, the mountain to yield. 21 successes would make First and Forsaken Lion stay his armies for a single day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T03:55:14-07:00","id":1320075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1319901#post1319901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You either succeed or you don't. Aside from extended rolls (let's include combat in that), bonus successes don't do anything.As DrLoveMonkey says, it's so you can succeed the hardest tasks in the most difficult circumstances reliably. I'd go one further and just let the player spend the motes and succeed without rolling most of the time.<br /> <br /> If you're trying to pick a lock, you either open the lock or you don't. A normal lock made by an average locksmith might be difficulty 1, while a magic lock created by a demi-god from a bygone age might be difficulty 5. Without a very good reason, I wouldn't put a Difficulty above 5 -- if it can't be done with five successes then it can't be done (without using magic).<br /> <br /> Conceptually, leaping ten stories or hearing tectonic plates move might be difficulty 20, but I straight up wouldn't allow a roll unless you had some kind of magic (not an Excellency) to facilitate it. And if you do have such magic, chances are the difficulty is going to be lower.<br /> <br /> 21 successes should be ridiculous overkill. (Or massive unprecidented progress on an extended roll.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually thought a lot about your answer and I kinda like it, it would help me a lot managing the power of excellencies that sometimes bother me. However I still have some unresolved issues with the limitations of difficulty at 5 : what happens when someone tries to open the aforementionned crafted by a demi god lock while the palace is crumbling around ? Is it still difficulty 5 ? The problem I have is the same of you fix the ceiling of difficulty higher : anything difficulty N would be difficulty N+1 under some circomstance, so defining a hard ceiling seems impossible. However I think the ceiling difficulty 5 is too low and doesn't allow for good adjustment, that I dont know how to resolve. Furthermore, there is an example of difficulty 10 state a fact in Miracles of the Solar Exalted, which made me think difficulty 5 is not the hard ceiling it seems to be in the core book","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T11:00:46-07:00","id":1320116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320075#post1320075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually thought a lot about your answer and I kinda like it, it would help me a lot managing the power of excellencies that sometimes bother me. However I still have some unresolved issues with the limitations of difficulty at 5 : what happens when someone tries to open the aforementionned crafted by a demi god lock while the palace is crumbling around ? Is it still difficulty 5 ? The problem I have is the same of you fix the ceiling of difficulty higher : anything difficulty N would be difficulty N+1 under some circomstance, so defining a hard ceiling seems impossible. However I think the ceiling difficulty 5 is too low and doesn't allow for good adjustment, that I dont know how to resolve. Furthermore, there is an example of difficulty 10 state a fact in Miracles of the Solar Exalted, which made me think difficulty 5 is not the hard ceiling it seems to be in the core book</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you recall the exact context in Miracles? Difficult 5 isn\u2019t a hard ceiling technically (combat and social interactions can get to 9-10) but otherwise, what your describing is a source of penalties, more than a difficulty increase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T12:48:57-07:00","id":1320136,"title":"","content":"Yeah I found it again. Hundred Sages Focus, one of the new charm of Lore page 17, on its comment, has the writer (I don't know his legitimacy concerning the system though) wrote that he prepared an especially difficult secret to find with a lore roll Difficulty 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T13:16:44-07:00","id":1320140,"title":"","content":"I think, though I'm not sure, that the Lore charms were written by John Morke, who was at that time one of the two lead developers for Exalted 3rd edition.<br /> They certainly read like Morke's style.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I feel the game works as-is intended when anything that a normal human could possibly do is difficulty 1-5. Difficulty is something which is challenging but doable for one of the best people at it in the entire world (ie a difficulty 5 Athletics+Strength roll to lift something is the sort of challenge you get on &quot;World's Strongest Man&quot;; possibly not the final challenge though, that might be difficulty 6). Things which a human couldn't really do at all without modern technology, but which you want to allow your players to do with their incredible skill, could possibly be higher. But generally, I'd only use higher difficulties for magical stuff.<br /> (Of course, there's a lot of magical stuff in Exalted...)<br /> <br /> I think some of the examples given (for example, the appendix removal) are bad examples though, tbh. It's better to think:<br /> Challenging for an amateur, or easy but not effortless for a professional; difficulty 1-2<br /> Challenging for a professional, or easy but not effortless for the world champion; difficulty 3-4<br /> Challenging for the world champion; difficulty 5<br /> Extremely difficulty for the world champion; difficulty 7 (but there's very little that's going to be this difficulty, yet actually still possible without magic)<br /> <br /> This is based on the dice pools people are rolling, basically.<br /> <br /> The thing is, of course, that with an excellency, Solars can be world champions (ie have 9-11 dice) in multiple areas. Which is maybe story-appropriate (what is Batman not a world champion in?), but can be irritating for an ST to run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T13:34:58-07:00","id":1320142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320116#post1320116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you recall the exact context in Miracles? Difficult 5 isn\u2019t a hard ceiling technically (combat and social interactions can get to 9-10) but otherwise, what your describing is a source of penalties, more than a difficulty increase.</div> </div> </div> </div>The context is a charm that uses larceny to introduce a fact about the security weaknesses in a building. If the Storyteller determines that those facts are invalid because there simply are no weaknesses, then a difficulty 10 roll introduces one anyway.<br /> <br /> I don''t know if 5 should be considered a rock hard cap, but it's pretty firm. At a certain point though difficulty N+1 just enters territory of specific charms. There's a few reasons why I think that should be the case.<br /> <br /> For one it invalidates a lot of Solar charms, even ones that aren't low essence. A pretty stats dedicated Solar with a stunt and a full excellency, maybe some willpower in an emergency, can hit difficulty 9-10 fairly reliably. If you're letting the truly, utterly impossible tasks to happen at difficulty 10, then leaping from the ground to fly up to an airship flying high overhead is just the work of an Essence 1 dice adder and not an Essence 3 flight charm.<br /> <br /> Another is that there becomes little reason not to just go crazy with every roll. If you're infiltrating a palace and rolling to listen for guards on the other side of the door, difficulty 2, and you drop down 23 dice and double 8s on the roll, getting 14 successes, that's not a waste because you've just used sonar hearing to read the ink on the scrolls in the drawer of the satrap 5 stories above your head and can just leave now. Which also puts a ton of pressure on the ST when you have to think up some insane benefit for rolling 11 successes on a difficulty 1 lockpicking check.<br /> <br /> And for another it starts to muddy the identity of each type of exalt, and Solars in particular. For example, if you allow a Solar to, with a difficulty 10 roll, whisper into the wind and have it ride through the air to ears a mile away then that's no longer a cool unique thing that DBs can do with Wind Carried Words, it's something anyone exalt can do if they pump their linguistics exellency. The reason that this is even worse for Solars is because their feats often involve much less obvious and pure magic than something like WCW, and thus seem like their difficulty should be lower.<br /> <br /> Lets say there is a Dynast that's going to speak to her people, raising an army from her lands to go and carve a bloody path of conquest through neighboring kingdoms. You want to stop this but you don't have the chance to counter that speech with your own, they wouldn't let you get two words out before a fight started and scattered the crowds, and anyway you're a better dancer than a talker by far. So you sneakily convince her that you're part of a dance troupe and will perform before her speech to the people, and, somehow through dance, you're going to start a revolution.<br /> <br /> From a logic side of things, that would seem like a way easier difficulty roll than Wind Carried Words. You might set that at difficulty 6-7, since it's impossible by mortal standards, but it doesn't seem absurd. Actually though, that kind of emulates the charm Penultimate Unity of Form, which is an Essence 3 Solar charm and costs a willpower. So now that ability to do the impossible and make a beautiful dance to have the same effect as Charlie Chaplain's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ibVpDhW6kDQ\" target=\"_blank\">speech</a> from the Dictator isn't an awesome thing that Solars get to do that sets them apart, it's something any exalt can do with an excellency and maybe a stunt or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, it's one of the reasons that I find Solars difficult to run, they just so easily blow past difficulty 5 that most difficulties are nearly meaningless to them. My experience with DBs is a lot better, but suffers a bit from the same problems even then. Thank god they don't get a million free excellencies...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, everyone's game is different and can do whatever you want, but if you want a true idea of the scale of Exalted, I don't think you should be looking at successes and what they mean, because they might mean nothing. Look at charms like Titan-Straightening Method and Nine Aeons Thew, stuff like that lets you grab and throw monsters who are thousands of feet tall. See the sidebar on page 274 of the coreboook for that. Or Ephemeral Induction Technique, which lets you reach out and form a spirit out of nothing but her own will to birth a being into the world. Or how about Soaring Pegasus Style, which just straight up lets a Solar make a horse fly, <i>that's</i> the scale of Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 06-22-2019, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T14:33:39-07:00","id":1320148,"title":"","content":"So I'll have few answers here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320116#post1320116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you recall the exact context in Miracles? Difficult 5 isn\u2019t a hard ceiling technically (combat and social interactions can get to 9-10) but otherwise, what your describing is a source of penalties, more than a difficulty increase.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I'm respecting the intent of the system augmenting the difficulty instead of putting maluses. Indeed, the Corebook suggests increasing difficulties when there are situationnal complications and the number of successes required is not set by some static value. Examples given are that lockpicking is difficulty 1, and lockpicking <b>at night </b>is difficulty 2. If there was some sort of opposed roll I'd go for maluses, but here this is not the case I believe.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> : I mostly agree with you, but the thing is it asks a tremendous amount of work from the ST and from players to be on an even ground on what you could expect from successes only and from charms. To Solar in particular, since you noted they feel less &quot;magical&quot;. My simple example would be Athletics : In the corebook, one of the example given is the one of running 3 days without stopping. At first I thought &quot;Well it's weird I'd rather see it as a charm, it's obvious no human can do that&quot;, except well that after some googling there are apparently some people that did that ! But then, and without being nitpicky, you have many questions to solve concerning difficulties : Is running for 3 days straight in the cold of Hell difficulty 6 ? Is running for 20 days straight humanly impossible and thus can only be achieved only with charm ? Do I really want to answer my player who bought all the athletics charm as an Athletics Supernal &quot;You just can't do it despite you buying every single charm about running, even the one where you are litteraly considered a battle group because you go so fast, because you didn't pay a charm that doesn't exist and let you run forever&quot;. What would be the damn design of such a charm ?<br /> <br /> And this is only to question one of the most straightforward situation with one of the most straightforward ability of the game. I don't want to conceive my difficulties in the game by learning what all the charms in the game do and then deducing what players can do through successes alone.<br /> <br /> I must say that most of the time I don't face questions so complicated during the game, and if I do I solve without too much problems. But from a pure design perspective, few guidelines on how to balance roll difficulties vs how you expect charms to solve problems would be very helpful.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a> The first time playing Exalted, after coming from some editions of Mages where people are kinda powerful but not all too powerful, I must say the power of the Solars is not so easy to handle","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 06-22-2019, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T15:53:32-07:00","id":1320157,"title":"","content":"I will try to answer each individually<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320148#post1320148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is running for 3 days straight in the cold of Hell difficulty 6?</div> </div> </div> </div>Running for 3 days straight in an icy hell would still be difficulty 5, but you now have to contend with the severe cold, which deals 1 bashing damage every hour that you sit in it, unless you make the (Stamina + Resistance) roll. By the book that's a difficulty 1 roll, but in more extreme environments it might be 2-3, or higher damage, or both. Considering that's a roll that you're making every hour you actually need quite a few dice to ensure that you won't die. The better way for a Solar to get around that is to just pick up a survival charm or two and just totally ignore that environmental hazard all together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320148#post1320148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is running for 20 days straight humanly impossible and thus can only be achieved only with charm ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Again, just by the rules I'm not saying anyone who wants to do it the other way is wrong and will have a bad time doing it, but feats beyond the abilities of the greatest mortals usually require a charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320148#post1320148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I really want to answer my player who bought all the athletics charm as an Athletics Supernal &quot;You just can't do it despite you buying every single charm about running, even the one where you are litteraly considered a battle group because you go so fast, because you didn't pay a charm that doesn't exist and let you run forever&quot;. What would be the damn design of such a charm ?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely something that can happen. Solars especially have hundreds and hundreds of charms, but even they don't have a charm for everything a character might want to do. For example there is no Solar linguistics charm that allows them to convey complex and complete information in one single symbol. Like imagine if just looking at the symbol for a radioactive hazard gave you an instantaneous and fairly comprehensive understanding of what neutron-gamma-alpha-beta ect. radiation was and the basics of how to protect yourself. Distance, lead shielding or thick stone walls in a pinch, stuff like that.<br /> <br /> That really seems like a Solar charm, but as far as I know, there isn't one matching that description written down in any of the books. Even if it is somewhere and I missed it though, it could easily not have been. It <i>is</i> still a charm effect though, and it falls on the player and the ST to work out exactly how the charm will work before they take it.<br /> <br /> It's just like if your player had taken all the running and feats of strength charms, but absolutely none of the jumping ones, and then wanted to attempt Mountain Crossing Leap style feats, or Eagle Wing Style ones. He's the flash for speed, and can hurl a stone tower over a mighty river, but leaping just isn't in his game. Which seems strange, and it's strange to me that they'd be so focused a character, but it's also strange how he has the power to crush a granite pillar with his bare hands, but if he has brawl and dex both at zero and one respectively he's not a good fist fighter. It's a bit of an oddity but that's how the game works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320148#post1320148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is only to question one of the most straightforward situation with one of the most straightforward ability of the game. I don't want to conceive my difficulties in the game by learning what all the charms in the game do and then deducing what players can do through successes alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is, the straightforwardness and simplicity of your example is actually the part that's making it the most confusing, I think. Because if a player asked how many successes they'd need on a Dex + Melee roll to reach into their soul and pull forth a blade of pure sunlight (lets assume Glorious Solar Saber didn't already exist) then there would be no question, that isn't a roll, that's a charm. Running for 10 straight days without rest is just so almost barely kind of possible that it feels like maybe that doesn't need to be a charm, but it does.<br /> <br /> Again again though, everyone should do what makes a good game for them, if you want to even go so far as to say that no charm but the excellency exists, and all charm effects are just difficulty levels and that works, then do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320148#post1320148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that most of the time I don't face questions so complicated during the game, and if I do I solve without too much problems. But from a pure design perspective, few guidelines on how to balance roll difficulties vs how you expect charms to solve problems would be very helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely agree, there's people a lot more experienced with Exalted than I am who have difficulties in this area.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T17:15:08-07:00","id":1320171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320140#post1320140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think some of the examples given (for example, the appendix removal) are bad examples though, tbh. It's better to think:<br /> Challenging for an amateur, or easy but not effortless for a professional; difficulty 1-2<br /> Challenging for a professional, or easy but not effortless for the world champion; difficulty 3-4<br /> Challenging for the world champion; difficulty 5<br /> Extremely difficulty for the world champion; difficulty 7 (but there's very little that's going to be this difficulty, yet actually still possible without magic)</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally like the way that the game establishes difficulty 1 as a thing that is standard fare for somebody heroic, and scales up from there. Both for the manner in which it establishes a baseline for what kinds of things should even call for a roll, and general tone of the action. The way that I read it is that it's more concerned with the dramatic context of any given action.<br /> <br /> I'm not really fond of the idea of tying conceptions of difficulties to skill levels because I like to emphasize the point that a character of any Attribute and Ability level is theoretically capable of achieving any difficulty. It emphasizes the point that heroism is not a matter of capability.<br /> <br /> With spending Willpower, an exceptional stunt, and maybe one or two other circumstantial bonuses, a character with 1s in the relevant stats has a chance of rolling five successes. I think that's the one that should be focused on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">21 successes would make First and Forsaken Lion stay his armies for a single day.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> 1: Good God, what has he done to get a Resolve of 20!<br /> <br /> 2: If those successes aren't pointed at an appropriate Intimacy, they can be five times as many and still be completely useless.<br /> <br /> ...Unless it's a bargain action, which sounds more like something that would get such a short reprieve, in which case you don't really need that many successes, but you do need something valuable to give him.<br /> <br /> In any case, the social system is one in which the basic difficulty system is kind of irrelevant, because difficulties are always always always the Resolve of the character whom you're trying to influence, and we've got a rather more firm system for what can be accomplished that is more concerned with intersecting characterisation and dramatic context rather than how high your numbers are.<br /> <br /> In that way, interaction with the First and Forsake Lion, with a high prince of Hell, why even with the Unconquered Sun himself can be a more dynamic and interesting thing than just relying on rolling absurd numbers. You know, regular people can interact with these characters so long as they have the correct lever. And if they don't, then nobody is going to care no matter how charmingly it is expressed. There are random peasants of the hinterlands who will be unmoved by 21 successes and no complementary Intimacy or similar.</span></span></span></div><br /> Your whole thing of everybody giving up swords? We have Intill and Persuade and (especially) Inspire actions to manage that in a coherent and accessible fashion.<br /> <br /> (You can't convince rain to do anything without magic because rain doesn't have Intimacies, consciousness, or a capacity to defy gravity)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Lets say there is a Dynast that's going to speak to her people, raising an army from her lands to go and carve a bloody path of conquest through neighboring kingdoms. You want to stop this but you don't have the chance to counter that speech with your own, they wouldn't let you get two words out before a fight started and scattered the crowds, and anyway you're a better dancer than a talker by far. So you sneakily convince her that you're part of a dance troupe and will perform before her speech to the people, and, somehow through dance, you're going to start a revolution.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">From a logic side of things, that would seem like a way easier difficulty roll than Wind Carried Words. You might set that at difficulty 6-7, since it's impossible by mortal standards, but it doesn't seem absurd. Actually though, that kind of emulates the charm Penultimate Unity of Form, which is an Essence 3 Solar charm and costs a willpower. So now that ability to do the impossible and make a beautiful dance to have the same effect as Charlie Chaplain's </span></span></span></div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ibVpDhW6kDQ\" target=\"_blank\">speech</a><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> from the Dictator isn't an awesome thing that Solars get to do that sets them apart, it's something any exalt can do with an excellency and maybe a stunt or something.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Ehhh, I don't think that's the best example. Regular Performance actions employing dance can't be as precise as that Solar Charm to make them cross-applicable, but one still has the option of Inspire actions to provide some manner of confusion or weaken their resolve to act. It's fantastical, but not explicitly magical; still within the range of the pulpy heroics that are the common dramatic fare of the system and setting.<br /> <br /> A Solar Charm accomplishes one's ends through a superficially similar method with superior efficiency and precision. But stuff like that ought to be happening in the setting without the presence of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Sure dancing in front of an army is easier than Wind Carried Words, while that Charm can do things like carry sentiments and instructions to people that are very far away from you, which no form of heroic performance can accomplish at all.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T17:30:30-07:00","id":1320178,"title":"","content":"Although, thinking more about it, I suppose there's not much harm in letting a regular action that rolled a massive number of successes accomplish something kind of beyond the usual scope of the system.<br /> <br /> Because for one, you've definitely employed several Charms to become capable of that result in the first place, so it's already a bit magic.<br /> <br /> And for another, it's surely not coming up that often.<br /> <br /> It's like a working. Lots of things that can be done with spells can be achieved with workings, just far less efficiently or frequently. If you want to do it often and know where to learn it, you get the spell. If you want communicating with rain to be a thing you do rather than that thing you did once on your most blessed day, learn a Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T22:49:21-07:00","id":1320205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320171#post1320171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhh, I don't think that's the best example. Regular Performance actions employing dance can't be as precise as that Solar Charm to make them cross-applicable, but one still has the option of Inspire actions to provide some manner of confusion or weaken their resolve to act. It's fantastical, but not explicitly magical; still within the range of the pulpy heroics that are the common dramatic fare of the system and setting.<br /> <br /> A Solar Charm accomplishes one's ends through a superficially similar method with superior efficiency and precision. But stuff like that ought to be happening in the setting without the presence of the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Inspire certainly, I should have been more clear though I think. I was imagining more an instill action, one that might instill people with a particular and carefully worded intimacy, or perhaps even more than one over the course of the dance. Something like &quot;Our current leaders never have our best interests at heart.&quot; and/or &quot;I live by the happiness of my neighbor, not their misery.&quot; Which is I think beyond even the ability of the heroic mortals of the world of Exalted to convey with a dance alone.<br /> <br /> I think it would be a lot more effective than most inspire actions. You could inspire them with calmness maybe, which would make them a bit sluggish and difficult to rouse to war, but it wouldn't make them suspicious of their leaders or aid you in sparking a bloody rebellion either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320178#post1320178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, thinking more about it, I suppose there's not much harm in letting a regular action that rolled a massive number of successes accomplish something kind of beyond the usual scope of the system.<br /> <br /> Because for one, you've definitely employed several Charms to become capable of that result in the first place, so it's already a bit magic.<br /> <br /> And for another, it's surely not coming up that often.<br /> <br /> It's like a working. Lots of things that can be done with spells can be achieved with workings, just far less efficiently or frequently. If you want to do it often and know where to learn it, you get the spell. If you want communicating with rain to be a thing you do rather than that thing you did once on your most blessed day, learn a Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was thinking of mentioning the same thing. It's really hard for a player to know beforehand that they want to do something so when it comes up it feels punishing to go &quot;Well that would be really nice if you had a charm for that, it's just too bad you don't&quot; especially when that's totally something their character would do if there was an available charm.<br /> <br /> I would only worry about players eventually just relying on that when really they should be grabbing a lot of the charms that do that. So like maybe the first time or two you can get a legendary 8-10 successes and after an hour's treatment convert all the patient's aggravated damage to lethal, saving the day and somehow curing whenever poor Chernobyl victim has crossed your doctor's doorstep, but after that you should really consider getting Wound-Cleansing Meditation or Grievous Wound Alteration Energy.<br /> <br /> Hmm, actually, a way to do that might be to go and look at available charms and see if you can't like, tone down what you're allowing to still make that a good option if you can. Like, maybe your medicine roll has a threshold difficulty of 5, and it converts a number of levels past that into lethal? That way even Grievous Wound Alteration Energy is still attractive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T23:38:32-07:00","id":1320208,"title":"","content":"Suspicion is an emotion, I see no reason to believe someone couldn\u2019t Inspire you with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T02:11:07-07:00","id":1320227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320157#post1320157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will try to answer each individually<br /> <br /> Running for 3 days straight in an icy hell would still be difficulty 5, but you now have to contend with the severe cold, which deals 1 bashing damage every hour that you sit in it, unless you make the (Stamina + Resistance) roll. By the book that's a difficulty 1 roll, but in more extreme environments it might be 2-3, or higher damage, or both. Considering that's a roll that you're making every hour you actually need quite a few dice to ensure that you won't die. The better way for a Solar to get around that is to just pick up a survival charm or two and just totally ignore that environmental hazard all together.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes. Again, just by the rules I'm not saying anyone who wants to do it the other way is wrong and will have a bad time doing it, but feats beyond the abilities of the greatest mortals usually require a charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is definitely something that can happen. Solars especially have hundreds and hundreds of charms, but even they don't have a charm for everything a character might want to do. For example there is no Solar linguistics charm that allows them to convey complex and complete information in one single symbol. Like imagine if just looking at the symbol for a radioactive hazard gave you an instantaneous and fairly comprehensive understanding of what neutron-gamma-alpha-beta ect. radiation was and the basics of how to protect yourself. Distance, lead shielding or thick stone walls in a pinch, stuff like that.<br /> <br /> I absolutely agree, there's people a lot more experienced with Exalted than I am who have difficulties in this area.</div> </div> </div> </div>We didn't understand each other completely I think, but I think you are mostly right in your answers so I'll pass quickly to lighten my points.<br /> <br /> My first example was basically &quot;Take a difficulty 5 roll and add some modifier in accord with the other difficulties presented to make it difficulty +1&quot;.<br /> <br /> My second example was more like : I found out that some people could run for 2-3 days, but I think it might even be more. So is 5 of running a charm ? Is 6 days a Charm ? At what point does it become a charm ? But I guess it's a question every type of game has one way or the other, not specifically Exalted, and I should just go along the flow of the game and deal with it with the context when it happens.<br /> <br /> But your answwers make sense and I think I'm trying to hard to solve problems that I actually deal with during my games without even realizing, so I should just keep going. I'll try the &quot;No charm no inhuman action&quot;, because Excellencies makes you excellent, that is the best of what humans can do, but only of what humans can do, and I kinda like the idea of doing that as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T02:30:20-07:00","id":1320233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320171#post1320171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally like the way that the game establishes difficulty 1 as a thing that is standard fare for somebody heroic, and scales up from there. Both for the manner in which it establishes a baseline for what kinds of things should even call for a roll, and general tone of the action. The way that I read it is that it's more concerned with the dramatic context of any given action.<br /> <br /> I'm not really fond of the idea of tying conceptions of difficulties to skill levels because I like to emphasize the point that a character of any Attribute and Ability level is theoretically capable of achieving any difficulty. It emphasizes the point that heroism is not a matter of capability.<br /> <br /> With spending Willpower, an exceptional stunt, and maybe one or two other circumstantial bonuses, a character with 1s in the relevant stats has a chance of rolling five successes. I think that's the one that should be focused on.<br /> <br /> 2: If those successes aren't pointed at an appropriate Intimacy, they can be five times as many and still be completely useless.<br /> <br /> In any case, the social system is one in which the basic difficulty system is kind of irrelevant, because difficulties are always always always the Resolve of the character whom you're trying to influence, and we've got a rather more firm system for what can be accomplished that is more concerned with intersecting characterisation and dramatic context rather than how high your numbers are.<br /> <br /> In that way, interaction with the First and Forsake Lion, with a high prince of Hell, why even with the Unconquered Sun himself can be a more dynamic and interesting thing than just relying on rolling absurd numbers. You know, regular people can interact with these characters so long as they have the correct lever. And if they don't, then nobody is going to care no matter how charmingly it is expressed. There are random peasants of the hinterlands who will be unmoved by 21 successes and no complementary Intimacy or similar.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I guess this is where different people have different expectations for the game !<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the butcher warrior not being able to save his wounded friend at all because, no matter how hero\u00efc he always proved to be, he never took the time to wonder if he would have to save someone instead of killing him. For me, &quot;Not being able to do it no matter how hard you try&quot; is also a very important source of drama, and I really like to use it during my games, not for everything of course, but enough when it is with the themes oh the character (interacting with his intimacies or against his intimacies&quot;<br /> <br /> The second point about the Social with intimacies was really the hardest to teach players that come from other games. I had so many times my players saying &quot;I rolled 20 successes on presence !&quot; and me answering &quot;Congratulations that doesn't work&quot;, when you are not used to it players really have a hard time figuring it out, but I think it makes the system have really good social interactions<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T04:46:45-07:00","id":1320245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320171#post1320171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally like the way that the game establishes difficulty 1 as a thing that is standard fare for somebody heroic, and scales up from there. Both for the manner in which it establishes a baseline for what kinds of things should even call for a roll, and general tone of the action. The way that I read it is that it's more concerned with the dramatic context of any given action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Standard fare in the sense that they'll almost certainly succeed, or that it's something challenging for someone heroic (in this area)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not really fond of the idea of tying conceptions of difficulties to skill levels because I like to emphasize the point that a character of any Attribute and Ability level is theoretically capable of achieving any difficulty. </div> </div> </div>Well, sure, but we need some kind of way to work out how difficult it is. We need to look at what's generally going to happen, not what's average.<br /> <br /> So if the players want to, say, sail a boat through a storm successfully, I might think &quot;hmmm, I reckon that'd be tricky but possible for a professional sailor, and very hard for an amateur, so I'll go for 3&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like, an amateur singer could have a really good day, get really lucky, reveal hidden talents, and do an amazing performance.<br /> But they probably won't.<br /> It's possible, but challenging. That's why I said things like &quot;challenging&quot;, or &quot;easy but not effortless.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With spending Willpower, an exceptional stunt, and maybe one or two other circumstantial bonuses, a character with 1s in the relevant stats has a chance of rolling five successes. I think that's the one that should be focused on. </div> </div> </div>If, when deciding difficulties, I say &quot;well a person with 1s could potentially get 5 successes&quot; and focus on that, I'm going to massively over-estimate the difficulties for things, and my PCs are going to fail most stuff.<br /> Difficulties should be assigned more averagely. If the fat, short Twilight who never does any exercise does manage to get 5 successes on his Athletics roll by an incredibly lucky roll, it'll be impressive, and that's fine. But a lot of the time, he'll fail.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T05:04:54-07:00","id":1320250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320178#post1320178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, thinking more about it, I suppose there's not much harm in letting a regular action that rolled a massive number of successes accomplish something kind of beyond the usual scope of the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think generally it's fine as long as it's not stepping on the toes of other charms. (Though some charms let you do things without a roll, which maybe could be done with a really hard roll.)<br /> <br /> I try to think of extra benefits when people roll more successes, but sometimes there isn't really anything else to add. Especially when they get enormous amounts of successes (which I've only seen with Performance and Craft).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-23-2019, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T05:08:30-07:00","id":1320251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320233#post1320233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess this is where different people have different expectations for the game !<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the butcher warrior not being able to save his wounded friend at all because, no matter how hero\u00efc he always proved to be, he never took the time to wonder if he would have to save someone instead of killing him. For me, &quot;Not being able to do it no matter how hard you try&quot; is also a very important source of drama, and I really like to use it during my games, not for everything of course, but enough when it is with the themes oh the character (interacting with his intimacies or against his intimacies&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I got quite frustrated running an Essence 5 Solar game that the PCs could basically succeed at every roll. It really takes away drama.<br /> <br /> I recently started an Essence 1 Lunar game, and while of course the PCs are really got at their specific areas, there's a lot of areas where they're rolling 2-3 dice. One player said after the first game, &quot;That was really good, it was fun to actually fail rolls sometimes!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second point about the Social with intimacies was really the hardest to teach players that come from other games. I had so many times my players saying &quot;I rolled 20 successes on presence !&quot; and me answering &quot;Congratulations that doesn't work&quot;, when you are not used to it players really have a hard time figuring it out, but I think it makes the system have really good social interactions<br /> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, our Zenith took some time to get used to that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T07:08:57-07:00","id":1320263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320245#post1320245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Standard fare in the sense that they'll almost certainly succeed, or that it's something challenging for someone heroic (in this area)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something challenging to the mundane people whom nobody is ever playing, and run-of-the-mill for player characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need to look at what's generally going to happen, not what's average.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those sound like they mean the same thing.<br /> <br /> My main focus is on the line saying that Exalted characters are presumed to have confidence and competence. One dot in an Ability is defined as somebody who is trained and/or experienced, they're not weak in it; for dramatic purposes, they might be assumed to make up for competence with confidence where necessary. <br /> <br /> Going by the description of difficulty 1, there's always supposed to be something a bit exceptional about what is rolled for in a game, and it's something accessible to all characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the players want to, say, sail a boat through a storm successfully, I might think &quot;hmmm, I reckon that'd be tricky but possible for a professional sailor, and very hard for an amateur, so I'll go for 3&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's difficulty 2. That's the standard fare for heroes, taking place under duress. <br /> <br /> Maybe if it's an outright hurricane or the boat is of distinctly low quality it's difficulty 3.<br /> <br /> I mean, the difference between amateur and professional in this system is one die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, an amateur singer could have a really good day, get really lucky, reveal hidden talents, and do an amazing performance.<br /> But they probably won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the dramatic context of this performance?<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that if it's Performance intended for social purposes, as I suppose to be the common application of the Ability in actual gameplay, the difficulty is the Resolve of other characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, when deciding difficulties, I say &quot;well a person with 1s could potentially get 5 successes&quot; and focus on that, I'm going to massively over-estimate the difficulties for things, and my PCs are going to fail most stuff.<br /> Difficulties should be assigned more averagely. If the fat, short Twilight who never does any exercise does manage to get 5 successes on his Athletics roll by an incredibly lucky roll, it'll be impressive, and that's fine. But a lot of the time, he'll fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the difficulty corresponds to a specific obstacle that a character is engaging with, that exists separately from them.<br /> <br /> When subjects like this come up, I feel as though some people are talking about rolling dice in general and looking for their successes to create a result, but that's not how the system is designed. You encounter a dramatic challenge, that challenge has a difficulty, and a dice pool is rolled to see if the challenge is overcome.<br /> <br /> So difficulty 5 for Athletics goes towards leaping a chasm that is so wide that it's hardly conceivable that anybody could leap across it. The person with 5 in Attribute and Ability isn't supposed to treat it as trivial in character, even if mathematically it's not too daunting. The Twilight you're describing... doesn't have Athletics at all, so I think they might not actually be capable of making the attempt? I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> I don't know, I feel as though I'm arguing minutiae, but it's minutiae that puts me off because it feels like focusing on using the system to create an objective measurement of the functions of the setting rather than focusing on the dramatic underpinnings of the story that is being told.<br /> <br /> I suppose I could describe my objection in terms of not really liking it to be described in terms of professionals and amateurs because I find the difficulty descriptions to be saying that the lowest standard to pass is something that everyday professionals would struggle with because they aren't routine. That if you faced a professional person with the circumstances of an Exalted game, and it was their first time ever encountering such, then they would go into a bit of shock because they're not prepared to deal with something with such pressure.<br /> <br /> If dice are being rolled, whether or not the character is professional seems less important than them being motivated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think generally it's fine as long as it's not stepping on the toes of other charms.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Why? The value of the Charm is not undermined, because the odds of repeating that success are quite unlikely.<br /> <br /> That and, if I was the Storyteller, accomplishing something dramatic and uncanny on the basis of rolling a ridiculous number of successes is something you're only allowed to do once. Like, the specific thing you did, you can always do something a bit different with it.<br /> <br /> Buying a Charm means that you have the capability to do it all the time.<br /> <br /> It's like saying that winning the lottery ticket to go and see the original run of Hamilton on Broadway is the equivalent of having the means and connections to see it once a week.<br /> <br /> Just, step on the toes of the Charm, this one time. The Charm has robust feet, it will surely get over it.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T07:56:09-07:00","id":1320277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320263#post1320263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those sound like they mean the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a mistake because I was thinking about something else.<br /> <br /> I meant we should focus on what's generally going to happen, ie the average, not what's potentially possible with amazing rolls.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T08:17:31-07:00","id":1320280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320263#post1320263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's something challenging to the mundane people whom nobody is ever playing, and run-of-the-mill for player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's fine, it's what I was saying. Challenging for an amateur, easy for a professional, and due to the dots they have, PCs tend to have professional (or higher!) skills in most areas.<br /> It's only challenging for their weakest areas. For example, a difficulty 1 Lore roll is challenging (but doable) for the gladiator Dawn who was raised to only do combat and have no education, and so is just rolling his Intelligence of 2, but pretty trivial for most PCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My main focus is on the line saying that Exalted characters are presumed to have confidence and competence. One dot in an Ability is defined as somebody who is trained and/or experienced, they're not weak in it; for dramatic purposes, they might be assumed to make up for competence with confidence where necessary.<br /> <br /> Going by the description of difficulty 1, there's always supposed to be something a bit exceptional about what is rolled for in a game, and it's something accessible to all characters. </div> </div> </div>I'm not really seeing where you're disagreeing with me here?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's difficulty 2. That's the standard fare for heroes, taking place under duress.<br /> <br /> Maybe if it's an outright hurricane or the boat is of distinctly low quality it's difficulty 3.<br /> <br /> I mean, the difference between amateur and professional in this system is one die. </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the difficulty corresponds to a specific obstacle that a character is engaging with, that exists separately from them.<br /> <br /> When subjects like this come up, I feel as though some people are talking about rolling dice in general and looking for their successes to create a result, but that's not how the system is designed. You encounter a dramatic challenge, that challenge has a difficulty, and a dice pool is rolled to see if the challenge is overcome. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So difficulty 5 for Athletics goes towards leaping a chasm that is so wide that it's hardly conceivable that anybody could leap across it. The person with 5 in Attribute and Ability isn't supposed to treat it as trivial in character, even if mathematically it's not too daunting. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Twilight you're describing... doesn't have Athletics at all, so I think they might not actually be capable of making the attempt? I'm not sure. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they've just got their Strength of 2 dice. And you were saying that someone with 2 dice could get 5 successes. I mean, it's very, very unlikely, but it's possible. With a stunt and willpower, to show (genre-wise) that he's really putting in his all, and in this dramatic situation he managed it, although generally he wouldn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know, I feel as though I'm arguing minutiae, but it's minutiae that puts me off because it feels like focusing on using the system to create an objective measurement of the functions of the setting rather than focusing on the dramatic underpinnings of the story that is being told. </div> </div> </div>I mean, you could obviously rate difficulties on how easy you want it to be, if you're going for a more narrativist route.<br /> But I find that Solars have enormous skill in the areas they're supposed to, so that it doesn't really matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose I could describe my objection in terms of not really liking it to be described in terms of professionals and amateurs because I find the difficulty descriptions to be saying that the lowest standard to pass is something that everyday professionals would struggle with because they aren't routine. </div> </div> </div>But a professional generally wouldn't struggle with a difficulty 1 task. It wouldn't be 100%, because it's not routine, but they're generally going to succeed. I mean, if you look at the examples in the book, even a conscript or militia soldier has 4 dice in Senses, Tracking, Threaten and 5 dice in Stealth. Nomadic horsemen have 9 dice in tracking (!). The example merchant has 7 dice in social influence.<br /> So difficulty 1 is not something everyday professionals will struggle with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If dice are being rolled, whether or not the character is professional seems less important than them being motivated. </div> </div> </div>I mean yes, that is a factor in terms of stunts, willpower, and excellencies, but surely skill matters? And I can't see how it would work for an ST to assign difficulties based on, what, how motivated PCs are? That's why I find it easiest to think of whether an unskilled person would find it difficult, or a skilled person would find it difficult.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why? The value of the Charm is not undermined, because the odds of repeating that success are quite unlikely.<br /> <br /> That and, if I was the Storyteller, accomplishing something dramatic and uncanny on the basis of rolling a ridiculous number of successes is something you're only allowed to do once. Like, the specific thing you did, you can always do something a bit different with it.<br /> <br /> Buying a Charm means that you have the capability to do it all the time.<br /> <br /> It's like saying that winning the lottery ticket to go and see the original run of Hamilton on Broadway is the equivalent of having the means and connections to see it once a week.<br /> <br /> Just, step on the toes of the Charm, this one time. The Charm has robust feet, it will surely get over it.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR][/LEFT] </div> </div> </div>Yeah, as long as it's something that's just very occasional. That was what I meant by the part in brackets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T08:42:30-07:00","id":1320283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted#post1319165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while there are many charms that explain part of what a character does and how insane and impressive it is, the difficulty scale only really goes up to 5 in terms of descriptions, and many exalted in their specialty *vastly* exceed that, so... what the hell does 21 successes *mean?*</div> </div> </div> </div>I just sat down again and wondered about what you wrote. And then I applied math to what you said...<br /> To get 21 successes is a minimum of 11 dice (5 Attribute + 5 Ability + 1 Specialty), or 10 dice and a success with a willpower. The average on 10 dice is 5 successes, which is a 50/50 shot on making a difficulty 5 roll. <br /> And if he wants to really succeed, he's going to stunt for extra dice, use charms to add more dice, use charms to reroll low numbers and charms to get double successes on more high numbers, and basically spend to bunch of essence to make this roll (and then he rolled well to boot). <br /> The main thing is though, he took a roll that had about a 50/50 shot at blowing it if you were the best of the best (and way beyond average), and made it as easily as Solar's are supposed to do.<br /> <br /> And that's something to think about. Attribute 5 and Ability 5 have only a 50% chance at making a difficulty 5 roll without stunts and charms. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T08:57:20-07:00","id":1320289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320280#post1320280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PCs tend to have professional (or higher!) skills in most areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I feel as though this has been a point of dispute before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, they've just got their Strength of 2 dice. And you were saying that someone with 2 dice could get 5 successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of somebody with 1s. I wish the game had said something about attempting actions with no Ability dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you could obviously rate difficulties on how easy you want it to be, if you're going for a more narrativist route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not talking bout easiness, talking bout dramatic significance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a professional generally wouldn't struggle with a difficulty 1 task. It wouldn't be 100%, because it's not routine, but they're generally going to succeed. I mean, if you look at the examples in the book, even a conscript or militia soldier has 4 dice in Senses, Tracking, Threaten and 5 dice in Stealth. Nomadic horsemen have 9 dice in tracking (!). The example merchant has 7 dice in social influence.<br /> So difficulty 1 is not something everyday professionals will struggle with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about mathematics, I'm talking about characterisation. What did you think I was going on about when I talked about people freezing up?<br /> <br /> If the conscript has the presence of mind to manage anything at all in acting against the Exalted, then even just for that one moment they're a bit more heroic than most people in the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean yes, that is a factor in terms of stunts, willpower, and excellencies, but surely skill matters? And I can't see how it would work for an ST to assign difficulties based on, what, how motivated PCs are? That's why I find it easiest to think of whether an unskilled person would find it difficult, or a skilled person would find it difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oy, I find the idea of trying to answer this one to defeat what I'm willing to type from a phone.<br /> <br /> Or possibly at all; I feel as though you don't understand what I'm talking about at all (by which I mean a fundamental difference in perspective that results in misunderstanding of my statements), and the prospect of trying to resolve that in this medium of communication feels distinctly exhausting.<br /> <br /> I'll just ask you to tell me how you read the core book's description of the difficulty levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T09:43:23-07:00","id":1320298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320289#post1320289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or possibly at all; I feel as though you don't understand what I'm talking about at all (by which I mean a fundamental difference in perspective that results in misunderstanding of my statements), and the prospect of trying to resolve that in this medium of communication feels distinctly exhausting.<br /> <br /> I'll just ask you to tell me how you read the core book's description of the difficulty levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I might include myself in your discussion, as extremely confusing, even for narrative purpose !<br /> <br /> I'll re-use the exampe of the &quot;removing the appendix&quot; from the patient, at difficulty 1. If it's so easy to do it that anyone can basically do it with 2-3 at most in stats (and furthermore willpower, stunts ...), when the fuck am I going to give the Greatest Warrior of the Sun the Limit Break of All-Consuming Grief because he failed to save his friend in time of need because he never prepared for that ?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T11:34:05-07:00","id":1320323,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Isator, no I haven't really been following you. Sorry. I don't really understand what your point is. That difficulties should be assigned by narrative significance?<br /> <br /> I'll have a look at the Core later if I have time, but I'm watching a film with my friends now and then playing Exalted (it's a crossover today).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T13:26:38-07:00","id":1320342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320298#post1320298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I might include myself in your discussion, as extremely confusing, even for narrative purpose !<br /> <br /> I'll re-use the exampe of the &quot;removing the appendix&quot; from the patient, at difficulty 1. If it's so easy to do it that anyone can basically do it with 2-3 at most in stats (and furthermore willpower, stunts ...), when the fuck am I going to give the Greatest Warrior of the Sun the Limit Break of All-Consuming Grief because he failed to save his friend in time of need because he never prepared for that ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what difficulties are for.<br /> GWotS has no medicine. So he has to figure out that his buddy has a burst appendix and was not poisoned. Diagnosis without medicine skill, -1 difficulty because GWofS doesn't even know what an appendix is. He gets to roll his 1 or 2 dice.<br /> Then he has to operate on his buddy, but without knowing exactly where the appendix is (except in general terms where his buddy is grabbing his midsection), and without proper equipment. Maybe 2 -1 penalties? Now where is his dice pool? And if he blew the first roll, he doesn't even get this far.<br /> <br /> Yeah, he could make the difficulty 1 roll, but penalties are going to make it interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T13:26:38-07:00","id":1320343,"title":"","content":"Sorry, Double post.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T17:18:34-07:00","id":1320362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320298#post1320298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I might include myself in your discussion, as extremely confusing, even for narrative purpose !<br /> <br /> I'll re-use the exampe of the &quot;removing the appendix&quot; from the patient, at difficulty 1. If it's so easy to do it that anyone can basically do it with 2-3 at most in stats (and furthermore willpower, stunts ...), when the fuck am I going to give the Greatest Warrior of the Sun the Limit Break of All-Consuming Grief because he failed to save his friend in time of need because he never prepared for that ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, you are just going to have to find an opportunity to game when the person holding a gun to your head to force you to make dice rolls that are theoretically possible but not in keeping with your character intentions is out of reach.<br /> <br /> That or kill the person with something beyond the scope of regular Medicine actions such as a health track filled to bursting with lethal damage. Either or.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T21:50:46-07:00","id":1320404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320227#post1320227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We didn't understand each other completely I think, but I think you are mostly right in your answers so I'll pass quickly to lighten my points.<br /> <br /> My first example was basically &quot;Take a difficulty 5 roll and add some modifier in accord with the other difficulties presented to make it difficulty +1&quot;.<br /> <br /> My second example was more like : I found out that some people could run for 2-3 days, but I think it might even be more. So is 5 of running a charm ? Is 6 days a Charm ? At what point does it become a charm ? But I guess it's a question every type of game has one way or the other, not specifically Exalted, and I should just go along the flow of the game and deal with it with the context when it happens.<br /> <br /> But your answwers make sense and I think I'm trying to hard to solve problems that I actually deal with during my games without even realizing, so I should just keep going. I'll try the &quot;No charm no inhuman action&quot;, because Excellencies makes you excellent, that is the best of what humans can do, but only of what humans can do, and I kinda like the idea of doing that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I see now, I think. It's a bit of a problem of how fine a grain the system has. For example, running 3 days straight is difficulty 5, running 3.5 days straight, also probably difficulty 5, and same with 2.5 days straight. Once you get to the threshold that you'd think it should be something that's beyond that, then rather than become difficulty 6 it's probably so hard that you need a charm specifically for it.<br /> <br /> Now, Exalted is a world of heroes, even mortal ones, so they might be capable of doing just a bit more than people in real life, but it's not far off the mark. Then, remember, that people, some people, the very best examples of our species, are capable of some amazing things. Walking across Niagra Falls on <a href=\"https://i2-prod.mirror.co.uk/incoming/article886678.ece/ALTERNATES/s615/Tightrope%20walker%20Nik%20Wallenda%20walks%20the%20high%20wire%20from%20the%20U.S.%20side%20to%20the%20Canadian%20side%20over%20the%20Horseshoe%20Falls%20in%20Niagara%20Falls,%20Ontario\" target=\"_blank\">a tightrope</a>, freeclimbing <a href=\"https://www.kunc.org/sites/kunc/files/styles/x_large/public/201906/el_capitan_20180916.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">El Capitan</a> solo, freediving hundreds of meters, marathon runs in -30 degree centigrade weather, ect. Those are all near the range of difficulty 5 actions, maybe 4 for some of them, and they're all impressive as hell.<br /> <br /> If a Solar has some essence to throw into an excellency, and does a stunt, they do these things trivially, so that's still pretty epic and definitely nothing to just ignore. Like if there's really any chance that a human could perform the action, it's difficulty 5, but possible with an excellency.<br /> <br /> It might seem wasteful that a Solar can go so far beyond that, but it does come up sometimes. In contested rolls with the most powerful beings in the setting they might have to beat a roll of 5, for example, or simply just have 5 dice knocked off their roll for horrible penalties. It's just that when the book talks about Solars being so incredibly dexterous and agile that they can sprint straight up a smooth glass wall, it's talking about Spider Foot Style, not just a bunch of dice and willpower thrown at the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T04:08:57-07:00","id":1320451,"title":"","content":"I think there are a few things that might justify 6+ difficulty like feats of strength since they're just a matter of scale. Like jumping a chasm. That, I think, should be possible with only an excellency.<br /> <br /> Especially one that relies on attributes for it's dice cap. A lunar, for example, works by being stronger and faster than a mortal, not more skilled. So stronger legs should equal more jump power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-24-2019, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T07:44:39-07:00","id":1320490,"title":"","content":"So, Isator, you asked me to go back and look at the difficulty descriptions in the book, and say what I think about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core Book p.185</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tasks which runof-<br /> the-mill individuals in Creation would consider challenging<br /> (such as picking a lock or removing a patient\u2019s<br /> appendix without killing him) are ordinary fare for heroes.<br /> Such tasks are appropriate for difficulty 1.<br /> <br /> Performing challenging tasks under significant duress<br /> (such as picking a lock or removing an appendix in the<br /> dead of night, without sufficient light, in the midst of a<br /> howling storm) is appropriate for difficulty 2.<br /> <br /> Tasks which might daunt even heroes, by contrast, are<br /> appropriate for difficulty 3. Examples might include<br /> plucking a gem from a nest of writhing serpents without<br /> being bitten, or breaking a man-eating horse born in the<br /> depths of the Wyld so it accepts the hero as its rider.<br /> <br /> Performing such tasks under significant duress (such as<br /> plucking the aforementioned gem while the temple collapses<br /> around the intrepid thief, or breaking the maneating<br /> horse in the midst of a raging forest fire) are appropriate<br /> for difficulty 4.<br /> <br /> Near-impossible feats, even by heroic standards, are appropriate<br /> for difficulty 5. Examples might include reading<br /> a letter in pitch blackness by feeling the texture of ink on<br /> the paper, leaping over the rail of a sorcerer\u2019s flying chariot<br /> to land safely in a hay cart hundreds of feet below, or<br /> running for three consecutive days and nights without<br /> succumbing to exhaustion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than differentiating between 1 and 2, and differentiating between 3 and 4, which I didn't go into (as I'm writing posts, not rules), I'd say... yeah, that's basically what I was saying.<br /> <br /> Things a regular person finds challenging, but someone skilled finds ordinary (but not so ordinary as to mean you don't need to roll), is difficulty 1. Picking a lock is a good example. I've done it like once, it's pretty hard and took a while.<br /> <br /> Tasks which are challenging for very skilled individuals are difficulty 3. Both the examples look good.<br /> <br /> Tasks which are very difficult for very skilled individuals are difficulty 5. Again, seems good.<br /> I'll admit, it's a little more difficult-sounding than my gut feeling would go for; but maybe that's because I'm so used to games where PCs have 10 dice in a ton of stuff, and can excellency up past 10 dice in 90% of tasks, at which point these incredible feats become so humdrum as to become boring. Which feels wrong. But now I'm running a game where most players only have excellencies on less than half their rolls, and sometimes are only rolling 3 or 4 dice, it'll probably feel more impressive for people to succeed on difficulty 5 rolls, so they can and should be that epic.<br /> (I should say though, in practice, I virtually never assign things difficulty 5 unless the rules specifically call for it, so in reality I'm not really doing it any differently from the book.)<br /> <br /> I'd say the only problem I have with this section is, as I said in my first post, the one about taking out an appendix, which with pre-modern medicine I can't see famous and skilled doctors finding ordinary; the first appendectomy wasn't performed until the 1700s. No-one was doing them in the bronze age or even the Renaissance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-24-2019, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T08:35:29-07:00","id":1320500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1319993#post1319993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're playing 3e, if that helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you going to tell us what the roll pertains to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T10:32:36-07:00","id":1320525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320342#post1320342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what difficulties are for.<br /> GWotS has no medicine. So he has to figure out that his buddy has a burst appendix and was not poisoned. Diagnosis without medicine skill, -1 difficulty because GWofS doesn't even know what an appendix is. He gets to roll his 1 or 2 dice.<br /> Then he has to operate on his buddy, but without knowing exactly where the appendix is (except in general terms where his buddy is grabbing his midsection), and without proper equipment. Maybe 2 -1 penalties? Now where is his dice pool? And if he blew the first roll, he doesn't even get this far.<br /> <br /> Yeah, he could make the difficulty 1 roll, but penalties are going to make it interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not how the system is supposed to work, since the difficulty is given, not having proper medical equipment and now knowing where the appendix is should be an increase of difficulty, not a penalty to his roll.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, why doesn't he know where is the appendix ? Because he doesn't have medicine ? I don't think I'm supposed to give penalties to my player attempting to solve one problem because they don't have points in the Ability. The same way I wouldn't raise difficulty for opening a lock from 1 to 2 because the character have 0 in Larceny. It would make sense to give inherent malus because you are poorly skilled in some other RPG, but I don't see this implied anywhere in Exalted 3e.<br /> <br /> And finally, indeed if he doesn't know what to do, he will indeed certainly fail, but that's not what the situation presented in the Corebook is, and that's my problem with it : Lack of context. I'm not a game developper so surely my example might be confusing as well, but I think &quot;Diagnosing someone with an appendix disease&quot; would have been a more clearer example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, you are just going to have to find an opportunity to game when the person holding a gun to your head to force you to make dice rolls that are theoretically possible but not in keeping with your character intentions is out of reach.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>C'mon don't &quot;Learn how to roleplay your character better&quot; me, I'm just asking lots of questions because I love this game, I've been playing it since I discovered it, and I really want to better my ST and player capacity, sorry if I got on your nerve by interrupting. I'm a Chosen of the Sun, imbued with the greatest power ever bestowed to mankind, filled with courage and valor from a glorious time, what do you want me to roleplay in this kind of situation ? Monologuing about &quot;I should have gone to med school like mom told me&quot; while my dearest friend is dying ? Of course I'm going to try for my best stunt and use a WP to try to save my friend, I've almost never encountered any single character for which it would make sense to not even try it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Solar has some essence to throw into an excellency, and does a stunt, they do these things trivially, so that's still pretty epic and definitely nothing to just ignore. Like if there's really any chance that a human could perform the action, it's difficulty 5, but possible with an excellency.<br /> <br /> It might seem wasteful that a Solar can go so far beyond that, but it does come up sometimes. In contested rolls with the most powerful beings in the setting they might have to beat a roll of 5, for example, or simply just have 5 dice knocked off their roll for horrible penalties. It's just that when the book talks about Solars being so incredibly dexterous and agile that they can sprint straight up a smooth glass wall, it's talking about Spider Foot Style, not just a bunch of dice and willpower thrown at the issue.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I was really nitpicky about the granularity of the system in my post, thanks for your patience. I still don't really like the idea of a hard-cap so low for non-confrontational rolls, because it creates strange system behaviors and strange expectations for what a good roll should be (like if in a contested roll A roll 12 successes and B rolls 15 successes, since they are anyway bound by the human limit, shouldn't they be in a tie because they can't achieve more than what is humanly possible ?) but that's my problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll admit, it's a little more difficult-sounding than my gut feeling would go for; but maybe that's because I'm so used to games where PCs have 10 dice in a ton of stuff, and can excellency up past 10 dice in 90% of tasks, at which point these incredible feats become so humdrum as to become boring. Which feels wrong. But now I'm running a game where most players only have excellencies on less than half their rolls, and sometimes are only rolling 3 or 4 dice, it'll probably feel more impressive for people to succeed on difficulty 5 rolls, so they can and should be that epic. </div> </div> </div>That's been my main problem with the game from the release. It really got better when I started telling my players what the difficulties were for the roll they were facing (I know it's written in the book to do that, but I completely forgot it for my 2 year campaign), and when I decided to try to &quot;granulate&quot; a bit more the problem my players encountered, to give them more substance and more possible twists and reversals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T11:53:11-07:00","id":1320540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320525#post1320525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I was really nitpicky about the granularity of the system in my post, thanks for your patience. I still don't really like the idea of a hard-cap so low for non-confrontational rolls, because it creates strange system behaviors and strange expectations for what a good roll should be (like if in a contested roll A roll 12 successes and B rolls 15 successes, since they are anyway bound by the human limit, shouldn't they be in a tie because they can't achieve more than what is humanly possible ?) but that's my problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't necessarily consider it a hard cap exactly, more like a pretty firm cap. You might push past it for certain things in rare circumstances. I just caution allowing too good of a roll to emulate other charms too well. Dragonblooded are my favourite splat in this game, but Solars really need to keep that feeling of just being straightforward, powerful superheroes. A Dragonblood using medicine, for example, can get 11 dice from stats, 6 from an excellency, which if maxed adds a bonus non-charm success, and a lot of their low essence charms let you double 9s, which on average adds 1 extra success for every 10 dice rolled.<br /> <br /> So, with that, a level 2 stunt and a willpower you're looking at about an average roll of around 15, if they're essence 5 and use Most Beneficent Seed of the Five Dragons, it's more like 25. If you're looking to match that to the difficulty scale when 1 was remove an appendix, and 2 is remove an appendix in the dead of night without adequate light in the midst of a howling storm, then 15 is probably looking along the lines of performing an hour's worth of treatment in the span of a couple of seconds, or maybe cure blindness, deafness, or allow for the regrowth of lost tissue. In the game though, those are Essence 2-3 Solar charm effects, things that even Solars can't do at chargen unless medicine is their one special thing. Many of those effects even cost more motes and willpower than the DB spent getting those successes.<br /> <br /> If Dragonblooded are able to do that from their chargen it just takes away a bit from how special Solars are. Which is okay, because DBs are special in their own ways, but we still have to draw the line somewhere, and putting it around where the greatest mortal heroes of Creation top out is a pretty decent place. That way every kind of exalt has the relative same starting baseline, and the developers can focus on making each one unique in their own special ways, with their own unique charms.<br /> <br /> For example the Essence 1 Dragonblooded charm that lets them convert levels of lethal to bashing over the course of six seconds. Solars don't get a charm that converts health levels so quickly until Essence 3, and it costs twice as much, and is only usable once per scene, and can't convert nearly as many health levels at once, the only benefit, which is quite good, is to heal bashing or lethal completely. The reason for this is because Dragonblooded medicine is not really like Solar medicine, in spite of it being way worse overall, it has a lot more elements of magic and manipulation. Solars are the greatest doctors in the universe, but Dragonblooded just dump a bunch of life essence into your veins, which closes all your open wounds in mere moments.<br /> <br /> So what do Solars get that's so cool that Dragonblooded don't? And I keep using Solars and DBs because they're polar opposite ends of the power scale, and I know them both better than Lunars right now. Well Solars can perform surgery without tools, using their incredible skill, they can even cure the blind, the deaf, crippled and even missing limbs. That's something Dragonblooded just can't do, believe it or not, in spite of their 25 success medicine rolls, and it's important to keep that distinction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For contested rolls you might even consider it a kind of granularity adder. At that point you're not really determining an upper limit, just who is slightly better. Like two exalts climbing a rock wall, if one gets 15 successes and the other only 5, the winner probably doesn't speed by the loser Roadrunner style, unless he's using Hare Racing Method, but he does solidly win that contest.<br /> <br /> If she IS using Hare Racing Method, or Godspeed Steps, or One Extra Step, or god help you all three combined, then yes, the Solar flashes to the top of the rock wall so quickly that only the supernaturally enhanced vision of other spiritually powerful beings would likely to even see that she moved at all, rather than just teleported.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T12:04:28-07:00","id":1320543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320525#post1320525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that's not how the system is supposed to work, since the difficulty is given, not having proper medical equipment and now knowing where the appendix is should be an increase of difficulty, not a penalty to his roll.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, why doesn't he know where is the appendix ? Because he doesn't have medicine ? I don't think I'm supposed to give penalties to my player attempting to solve one problem because they don't have points in the Ability. The same way I wouldn't raise difficulty for opening a lock from 1 to 2 because the character have 0 in Larceny. It would make sense to give inherent malus because you are poorly skilled in some other RPG, but I don't see this implied anywhere in Exalted 3e.<br /> <br /> And finally, indeed if he doesn't know what to do, he will indeed certainly fail, but that's not what the situation presented in the Corebook is, and that's my problem with it : Lack of context. I'm not a game developper so surely my example might be confusing as well, but I think &quot;Diagnosing someone with an appendix disease&quot; would have been a more clearer example.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because taking out an appendix is a difficulty 1 task. Cut the guy open, cut out the appendix, and sew the intestine and the hole. Tada.<br /> And as you pointed out, difficulties don't change. So what are penalties for? Things that hamper doing the task. The penalty isn't for not having medicine, the penalty is for going in blind. You don't know what you are looking for exactly, and you sort of know where it is because that's where he says the pain is. Is it a parasite? A curse? This red thing in a mass of other red things? -1 for blind.<br /> No proper tools? Once again, a penalty. Doing delicate cutting with a grand diaklave is some sort of penalty. If he were a doctor he would know just what to do, not having the proper tools wouldn't increase his difficulty, just create a penalty to operating.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, I made it into the separate tasks, which is what the rules say to do. Diagnosis is the first step. Removing the appendix is the second task. So really, &quot;remove the appendix&quot; is a difficulty 1 task.<br /> <br /> The diagnosis was added because you complained that you WANTED him to fail for angst. I tried to help you out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T12:28:20-07:00","id":1320549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320490#post1320490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Things a regular person finds challenging, but someone skilled finds ordinary</div> </div> </div> </div>Your conflation of skill with heroism unnerves me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the only problem I have with this section is, as I said in my first post, the one about taking out an appendix, which with pre-modern medicine I can't see famous and skilled doctors finding ordinary; the first appendectomy wasn't performed until the 1700s. No-one was doing them in the bronze age or even the Renaissance.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting of Exalted is modelled off of the Bronze Age, often superficially, but is not it. Relatively sophisticated medicine has always been its forte, going back to First Edition and statements from Geoff Grabowski.<br /> <br /> If it wasn't, what would the Medicine Ability even be for?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T12:35:45-07:00","id":1320552,"title":"","content":"As for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a>, if not a solution that is in keeping with the general functions of the setting, what are you even looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T12:53:51-07:00","id":1320559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320552#post1320552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24291\" data-vbnamecard=\"24291\">Chausse</a>, if not a solution that is in keeping with the general functions of the setting, what are you even looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know actually !<br /> <br /> When I see someone write &quot;Open a chest crafted from the litteral best crafter of the First Age should be Difficulty 5&quot;, it really tilts me (no offense intended) because I got the feeling I'm have going to have a problem as a ST because :<br /> <br /> - Either I do not accept the rules as they are, and say the crafter of my table &quot;Do a Craft roll/Larceny roll to set protections of the chest you crafted&quot; and I'm then distorting the rules<br /> <br /> - Either I follow the rules and then the Night of the group that want to sneak in and see what's in the chest will win over the crafter because he is not bound by the same rules than the other player, and thus I'm being unfair.<br /> <br /> I know the Orichalcum Rule says &quot;you can solve it by yourself&quot;, but I got lots of this kind of complicated cases where I don't even know how to begin with, and I feel like I'm taking a solution that is either being unfair to one of my player or to me (I just posted something in the &quot;How do you lie&quot; earlier that illustrates this)<br /> <br /> To be clear when I'm playing or mastering a game, I usually resolve the problem with some &quot;roll with it solution&quot;, and I accept it. But when I'm discussing the intrinsic functionning of the system, the lore, the world and the narrative, I want to go deep into the matter and get real advices on how to better myself, not just learn that I can &quot;roll stuff&quot; or &quot;The maximum difficulty is 5&quot;. I know sometimes it's annoying to other people because I'm pushy (I think that's the word), and I'm sorry for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T13:53:48-07:00","id":1320571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320559#post1320559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I see someone write &quot;Open a chest crafted from the litteral best crafter of the First Age should be Difficulty 5&quot;, it really tilts me (no offense intended) because I got the feeling I'm have going to have a problem as a ST because :</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so this could mean a lot of things. When you say the literal best crafter in the first age, do you mean the greatest and most storied Twilight caste locksmith? If that's the case, then there is definitely more going on with that locked box than just a 'simple' difficulty 5 roll.<br /> <br /> Firstly, if that box is an example of his finest work, it's probably going to be an artifact. One which doesn't just have one lock with a simple tumbler setup, but one with many locks, some that can only be opened in certain times of the year, or only when bathed in red light. For those kind of locks, to open them outside of their conditions, you'd need larceny charms. There might also be a few very very difficult almost mundane style locks in there with difficulties in the 6-7 range, although I think that would be pretty rare. You could also have a difficulty 5 one with the condition that if you fail to open the lock a demon escapes to destroy the trespasser.<br /> <br /> If it's just a mundane box though, then yeah, difficulty 5. But if he's a Solar lockpicker then he'll probably have Lock Opening Touch, it's a Larceny 1, Essence 2 charm with no prerequisites that lets you open any mundane lock without even rolling, regardless of difficulty. It could have difficulty 100 in the system and that charm would just open it with a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> Exalts in general, but Solars especially, generally just kind of take most of the setting and wave their hand at it dismissively until presented with something like an otherworldly creature capable of destroying a continent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 06-24-2019, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T14:56:52-07:00","id":1320582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320549#post1320549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your conflation of skill with heroism unnerves me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The setting of Exalted is modelled off of the Bronze Age, often superficially, but is not it. Relatively sophisticated medicine has always been its forte, going back to First Edition and statements from Geoff Grabowski.<br /> <br /> If it wasn't, what would the Medicine Ability even be for?</div> </div> </div> </div>In this particular example, I'm sure that's what they mean by heroic, they're just saying it in a fancy way.<br /> <br /> Unless you are arguing that stuff is literally just easier for heroes of equal skill to non-heroes? Are you talking about stunts and willpower? Because that's assigned after difficulties. Where does their skill come in? Doesn't this rather detract from the great doctor PC with Medicine 5 if the rolls for him would challenge another great doctor with equal skill but are trivial for him.<br /> <br /> Look, difficulties are rolled against with dots representing your skill. The more skill needed, the higher the difficulty.<br /> If you really want to say &quot;It should be easier for heroes!&quot;, well, they can stunt and spend willpower. Isn't that enough? Should they also get a lower difficulty?<br /> <br /> As to the medicine, sure, that's why it's not difficulty 5. Perhaps they can use herbs or chi points or kung-fu needle skill. Or the surgery skill that medieval doctors had (because many medical operations did exist prior to modern medicine that would be suitable examples, I roll medicine to stitch people up all the time).<br /> But for an example of the lowest difficulty roll on the game, it confuses many readers, as they start asking &quot;wait, isn't that a very difficult thing to do?&quot; As happened in this thread, and several others I've seen. So I think it's better to look at the main explanation than the example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T14:59:25-07:00","id":1320583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320559#post1320559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know actually !<br /> <br /> When I see someone write &amp;quot;Open a chest crafted from the litteral best crafter of the First Age should be Difficulty 5&amp;quot;, it really tilts me (no offense intended) because I got the feeling I'm have going to have a problem as a ST because :<br /> <br /> - Either I do not accept the rules as they are, and say the crafter of my table &amp;quot;Do a Craft roll/Larceny roll to set protections of the chest you crafted&amp;quot; and I'm then distorting the rules<br /> <br /> - Either I follow the rules and then the Night of the group that want to sneak in and see what's in the chest will win over the crafter because he is not bound by the same rules than the other player, and thus I'm being unfair.<br /> <br /> I know the Orichalcum Rule says &amp;quot;you can solve it by yourself&amp;quot;, but I got lots of this kind of complicated cases where I don't even know how to begin with, and I feel like I'm taking a solution that is either being unfair to one of my player or to me (I just posted something in the &amp;quot;How do you lie&amp;quot; earlier that illustrates this)<br /> <br /> To be clear when I'm playing or mastering a game, I usually resolve the problem with some &amp;quot;roll with it solution&amp;quot;, and I accept it. But when I'm discussing the intrinsic functionning of the system, the lore, the world and the narrative, I want to go deep into the matter and get real advices on how to better myself, not just learn that I can &amp;quot;roll stuff&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;The maximum difficulty is 5&amp;quot;. I know sometimes it's annoying to other people because I'm pushy (I think that's the word), and I'm sorry for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's probably important to know that opposed rolls specifically don't follow the normal way of assigning difficulty.<br /> So if two PCs are trying to beat each other, it's going to be a roll-off, the crafter isn't capped at 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T15:20:02-07:00","id":1320590,"title":"","content":"Wait, Isator, ignore what I said before, possibly this has come together in my brain (or I'm still not following you at all, but let's try).<br /> <br /> Would you be happy with these?:<br /> <br /> Difficulty 1 - Challenging but doable for a regular unskilled person.*<br /> <br /> Difficulty 3 - Really difficult for a regular unskilled person.**<br /> <br /> Difficulty 5 - Virtually impossible for a regular unskilled person.***<br /> <br /> *So pretty easy for an unskilled heroic person with a stunt<br /> <br /> **So challenging but doable for a unskilled heroic person with a stunt and maybe willpower<br /> <br /> ***So really difficult, but possible, for a really motivated unskilled but heroic person with a stunt and willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-25-2019, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T15:22:18-07:00","id":1320591,"title":"","content":"Is it written anywhere that 5 is actually a cap for difficulties? It just doesn't go above that in the explanation of what difficulties to set. Of course, it is written so in order to discourage people from using higher difficulties. However, there is a number of rolls against a static value whose difficulty explicitly goes above 5, notably Feats of Strength, <br /> <br /> I would just go for a higher difficulty, if inclined to do so. I essentially read the scale 1-5 in difficulty as a warning against inflation, not hard-and-fast rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T15:57:20-07:00","id":1320598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320298#post1320298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I might include myself in your discussion, as extremely confusing, even for narrative purpose !<br /> <br /> I'll re-use the example of the &quot;removing the appendix&quot; from the patient, at difficulty 1. If it's so easy to do it that anyone can basically do it with 2-3 at most in stats (and furthermore willpower, stunts ...), when the fuck am I going to give the Greatest Warrior of the Sun the Limit Break of All-Consuming Grief because he failed to save his friend in time of need because he never prepared for that ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay if I have a go?<br /> <br /> My Mistake - Already commented on - Nothing to see here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-24-2019, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T18:23:18-07:00","id":1320633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320591#post1320591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it written anywhere that 5 is actually a cap for difficulties? It just doesn't go above that in the explanation of what difficulties to set. Of course, it is written so in order to discourage people from using higher difficulties. However, there is a number of rolls against a static value whose difficulty explicitly goes above 5, notably Feats of Strength,<br /> <br /> I would just go for a higher difficulty, if inclined to do so. I essentially read the scale 1-5 in difficulty as a warning against inflation, not hard-and-fast rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that it's a hard cap exactly. Feats of Strength go up to 9 before you start needing charms to enhance your strength, some poisons have a duration measured in 10 intervals, there are some other examples from the books.<br /> <br /> From Arms of the Chosen for example there's an artifact strongbox that has a difficulty 7 lock, it's also difficulty 6 to subdue Stormcaller's rage through nothing more than sheer force of will. Even for artifacts though the difficulties aren't all that high, The Distaff's silken bindings are difficulty 4 to break through, peering into the stars to see someone's death is a difficulty 3 roll with Hawk Star.<br /> <br /> Even very powerful supernatural effects tend to max out around difficulty 5. Ahlat, the southern war god can inflict you with a horrible curse of endless bleeding without death, but that can be cured by a difficulty 5 (Dex + Medicine) roll. Octavian, the Living Tower, Quarter Prince of Hell can strike you with an awful black oil attack that kills your senses or your mind, but you can recover with a difficulty 5 (Sta + Resistance) roll as long as you have Exalted healing. Even resisting damage from laying on a pool of lava is only difficulty 5.<br /> <br /> So even really epic things tend not to require rolls beyond 5, although in some cases, and almost always magical ones, they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T20:08:53-07:00","id":1320642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320582#post1320582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this particular example, I'm sure that's what they mean by heroic, they're just saying it in a fancy way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I came back to this thread to say that I had realised that the difference between us was that I read the line as saying &quot;the baseline for actions that you bother to roll (and indeed, undertakings in gameplay generally) are extraordinary and audacious, out of keeping with what typical people engage in&quot;, where you are reading it as &quot;something that is kind of hard for people with low Abilities and pretty easy for those with high&quot;.<br /> <br /> But you've gotten ahead of me with things I'll want my laptop to respond to.<br /> <br /> For the time being, I'll say that quite apart from appealing to my own biases, I think my reading is more fitting to the tone of the game's narrative and system (which is inclined more towards drama than simulation), and matches an explanation Holden gave shortly after the book came out about why the difficulty was written like that.<br /> <br /> Edit: To ensure that there is no confusion, I am referring to this exchange:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On page 185, the book describes the difficulty appropriate in general rolls. However, it seems to make a difference between what heroes and &amp;quot;run-of-the-mill individuals&amp;quot; would find difficult. The way I read it, it implies a different (undisclosed) difficulty scale for normals. How does that work out?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nobody plays Bob the Janitor unless he's a secret kung-fu master, so scaling things for Random Townie #3 is mostly just something we opted not to care about. I mean, yeah, we could introduce another scale for the Foot Clan jobbers, but would that actually be worth the hassle of learning and using?<br /> <br /> edit: To unpack that thought, Second Edition spent a <i>lot of time</i> worrying about how well the mechanics represented the life of the setting, so to speak-- &amp;quot;do these rules reflect standard trade negotiations between the Guild and the Council of Entities? Does this look like the kind of haggling a citizen of Lookshy would do at the market? Will this produce results that reasonably replicate the historic survival rate of plague victims with access to only pre-modern medicine?&amp;quot; In other words, it was very concerned with holding up under thought exercises wherein NPCs used the system in their day-to-day lives.<br /> <br /> Third Edition spends almost no time at all caring about what happens when two NPCs interact without players' characters present, because the GM can just resolve that however it suits his story best. The system is calibrated to help the PCs participate in exciting stories, and really doesn't even try to do anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-24-2019, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T23:12:44-07:00","id":1320669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320642#post1320642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I came back to this thread to say that I had realised that the difference between us was that I read the line as saying &quot;the baseline for actions that you bother to roll (and indeed, undertakings in gameplay generally) are extraordinary and audacious, out of keeping with what typical people engage in&quot;, where you are reading it as &quot;something that is kind of hard for people with low Abilities and pretty easy for those with high&quot;.<br /> <br /> But you've gotten ahead of me with things I'll want my laptop to respond to.<br /> <br /> For the time being, I'll say that quite apart from appealing to my own biases, I think my reading is more fitting to the tone of the game's narrative and system (which is inclined more towards drama than simulation), and matches an explanation Holden gave shortly after the book came out about why the difficulty was written like that.<br /> <br /> Edit: To ensure that there is no confusion, I am referring to this exchange:<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so you want the basic things that PCs ever roll, at difficulty 1, to be pretty impressive stuff. With things that aren't very impressive unrolled. And I certainly see no reason for PCs to roll for routine stuff like cooking dinner or whatever. So I can get that, but there is a problem. I don't want to rush ahead and read in too much though, and you said you had more to write, so I'll just check; are we talking about PCs with great skill, or no real training in the area?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T02:23:17-07:00","id":1320696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320669#post1320669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so you want the basic things that PCs ever roll, at difficulty 1, to be pretty impressive stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not what I want, it's what the system is. Look at the things that I quoted; Weimann was on the same page as me, and Holden's response corroborates it and explains how and why it was the point.<br /> <br /> It rather handily covers your bugaboo about appendectomy and all; this isn't something that just any surgeon or physician in Creation would do, and when it's rolled (i.e. when it's a thing that characters in an actual story of the Exalted genre, rather than a routine procedure of non-existent medical drama games), it's something noteworthy, possibly even a bit improvised.<br /> <br /> I must say that having quickly found the Holden quote that effectively articulates and validates what I've been talking about diminishes my sense that I need any more elaborate argument going into minutiae of your statements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-25-2019, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-25T05:22:37-07:00","id":1320723,"title":"","content":"As long as you are happy and the OP who asked for advice is happy, sure. I gave him/her my advice, you disagreed, he/she can use whichever one seems more practical for their game. This is what works for me, it may not work in your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-25-2019, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T11:50:27-07:00","id":1321003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1320075#post1320075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually thought a lot about your answer and I kinda like it, it would help me a lot managing the power of excellencies that sometimes bother me. However I still have some unresolved issues with the limitations of difficulty at 5 : what happens when someone tries to open the aforementionned crafted by a demi god lock while the palace is crumbling around ? Is it still difficulty 5 ? The problem I have is the same of you fix the ceiling of difficulty higher : anything difficulty N would be difficulty N+1 under some circomstance, so defining a hard ceiling seems impossible. However I think the ceiling difficulty 5 is too low and doesn't allow for good adjustment, that I dont know how to resolve. Furthermore, there is an example of difficulty 10 state a fact in Miracles of the Solar Exalted, which made me think difficulty 5 is not the hard ceiling it seems to be in the core book</div> </div> </div> </div>5 is not a hard cap. You could push it to whatever you want.<br /> <br /> If the lock is normally difficulty 5, and you're picking it whilst vultures eat your eyes, with one hand behind your back, whilst the palace collapses around you then obviously that's going to be N+X difficulty (let's say 9).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't. I would rule that the task straight-up is impossible without charms. If the lock is so sophisticated/enchanted/difficult that it's already a difficulty 5 task, then any complicating factors are either going to be trivial (and thus not up the difficulty) or make the task &quot;impossible&quot; (even though a Solar with an Excellency probably could succeed &quot;on paper&quot; if you let them roll).<br /> <br /> It's like social combat. Just because you can roll 20 successes, doesn't make the task possible.<br /> <br /> But that's definitely a &quot;soft cap&quot;. If the roll is dramatically appropriate, I'd allow it. But routinely, if a normal person can't do it without magic then a Solar can't do it without magic. If the difficulty is more than five then it's probably not possible without magic.<br /> <br /> If it wouldn't challenge someone then it's usually not a roll. Routine stuff is difficulty zero. Something interesting is difficulty 1. Complicating factors can push that up to 5. Unless failure has dramatic consequences, I just assume the PCs will succeed. If the PC is chucking 11+ dice at removing Nameless NPC#244's appendix, then they succeed without a roll. If they're throwing 23 dice with double 7s, exploding 10s, and reroll 1s and 6s then I don't mind them auto succeeding on a difficulty 5 roll to remove that appendix without the proper tools in the dark during a hurricane.<br /> <br /> The challenge isn't the thing you overcome by throwing buckets of dice at. Solars are meant to be awesome. The challenge is the &quot;whys&quot; and &quot;what's nexts&quot;.<br /> <br /> Think of video games like Oblivian. When every faceless bandit &quot;levels up&quot; to match your capabilities there's no real sense of scale. I don't like building worlds where every random NPC has a lock crafted by the Unconquered Sun himself, and combat is only ever against Tyrant Lizards who turn out to be Lunars.<br /> <br /> Solars are meant to walk over Difficulty 5 tasks, and tasks aren't meant to be harder than Difficulty 5. This is why you're playing Exalted, not D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> Embrace the awesome.<br /> <br /> Your Solars are like Batman. If it can be done by a human in peak condition, then they can do it. No matter how hard or implausible it may seem.<br /> <br /> But if it can't be done, then it can't be done.*<br /> <br /> *until you chuck charms that make the impossible possible at it<br /> <br /> If the best human long jumper in the world can maybe jump a 29-foot-chasm on their best day as a once-in-a-lifetime achievement, then your podgy Dex 1 Athletics 0 Twilight gets to roll that difficulty 5 task. But if you want to jump 30-feet straight-up into the air, then you need a jumping charm, no matter how many successes you can roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-27-2019, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T07:12:27-07:00","id":1321162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321003#post1321003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 is not a hard cap. You could push it to whatever you want.<br /> <br /> If the lock is normally difficulty 5, and you're picking it whilst vultures eat your eyes, with one hand behind your back, whilst the palace collapses around you then obviously that's going to be N+X difficulty (let's say 9).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it differently. The difficulty 5 first age lock is difficulty 5, whether I'm doing it with all the time in the world and no one observing, or I'm doing it while vultures peck at my eyes in the middle of a volcanic eruption, while fighting off some insidious Yozi poison coursing through my veins. Its just that there is no penalty for the first roll, and a hefty penalty for the second one.<br /> I'm still going to do it, because I'm a Solar, and have charms to give me a dice pool that will crush the task.<br /> Difficulty 5 is a semi-firm cap for the task, and penalties are extra things added beyond the difficulty of the task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T07:30:05-07:00","id":1321164,"title":"","content":"If the difficulty is already set for the lock don\u2019t additional complications just add dice penalties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T07:46:53-07:00","id":1321165,"title":"","content":"According to the book, you generally only use penalties for when you can't put the difficulty up (say, opposed rolls). Otherwise you just raise the difficulty.<br /> I mean, not that it makes much difference either way, statistically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T08:34:31-07:00","id":1321173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321165#post1321165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the book, you generally only use penalties for when you can't put the difficulty up (say, opposed rolls). Otherwise you just raise the difficulty.<br /> I mean, not that it makes much difference either way, statistically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh I see I misremembered that section. I\u2019m honestly not sure I like that, there\u2019s a lot of charms that do things like ignore penalties due to certain things, just as an example, weather. If you just up the difficulty then that charm technically doesn\u2019t apply there, so your Clear Sight Through Thunder charm or whatever doesn\u2019t actually help you see an object through torrential rain, it only helps if you\u2019re trying to see past somebody\u2019s opposed stealth roll through the rain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T08:54:10-07:00","id":1321177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321173#post1321173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m honestly not sure I like that, there\u2019s a lot of charms that do things like ignore penalties due to certain things, just as an example, weather.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in those circumstances, using the charm would simply mean the difficulty was reduced. I wouldn't nerf a charm just because it wasn't, technically, a &quot;penalty&quot;. <br /> <br /> In general, I suspect that 3e has pushed things towards &quot;increase difficulty&quot; as opposed to &quot;reduce number of dice rolled&quot; because of the prevalence of dice tricks. Raising the difficulty by 1 may be mathematically equivalent to subtracting two dice, but only when you don't have some charm effect going on that gives you double 7s, or rerolls 5s, or something like that. Increasing the difficulty lets players use those dice tricks a bit more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T09:55:29-07:00","id":1321189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321173#post1321173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahh I see I misremembered that section. I\u2019m honestly not sure I like that, there\u2019s a lot of charms that do things like ignore penalties due to certain things, just as an example, weather. If you just up the difficulty then that charm technically doesn\u2019t apply there, so your Clear Sight Through Thunder charm or whatever doesn\u2019t actually help you see an object through torrential rain, it only helps if you\u2019re trying to see past somebody\u2019s opposed stealth roll through the rain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I honestly didn't realise that until I went back and reread it, because you're right.<br /> <br /> I think Kelly's suggestion is the best way to deal with it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T17:59:43-07:00","id":1321288,"title":"","content":"A big issue we have right now is that the core was done up by the previous developers who had a different paradigm when it came difficulty and penalties, which seems to have avoided penalties as much as possible. Both Dragon-blooded and lunars seem to have been written under a new paradigm which seems to operate at extremely low difficulties but with multiple sources of penalties.<br /> <br /> Until the new devs release the new core rules that DB's and lunars operate under we are going to have to keep patching up the holes as best we can.<br /> <br /> For what it is worth my group has used Kelly's solution to some success. Its not great but better than raw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T18:05:05-07:00","id":1321293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321288#post1321288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big issue we have right now is that the core was done up by the previous developers who had a different paradigm when it came difficulty and penalties, which seems to have avoided penalties as much as possible. Both Dragon-blooded and lunars seem to have been written under a new paradigm which seems to operate at extremely low difficulties but with multiple sources of penalties.<br /> <br /> Until the new devs release the new core rules that DB's and lunars operate under we are going to have to keep patching up the holes as best we can.<br /> <br /> For what it is worth my group has used Kelly's solution to some success. Its not great but better than raw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of like an Exalted 3.6, well it's not great but it's not terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T01:08:19-07:00","id":1321360,"title":"","content":"Exalted is extremely crunch heavy (ok you don't roll on a table to determine your AC, but between project slots and craft points, and how many types of XP and character resources I think that's a fair position to take). The preference for vague &quot;natural&quot; language instead of precise system terms and the massive changes between 2E and 3E, I think are more to blame than a shift of lead developers.<br /> <br /> In the corebook, Legend Soul Revival (p305) and the sidebar for its prereq talks of dice penalities rather than increased difficulty. Mind Cleansing Prana (p306) likewise removes upto -2 in penalities. Spirit Tempering Practice (p308) uses &quot;penalty&quot; in the natural language sense.<br /> <br /> The balance suggested by Mind Cleansing Prana is that negating -2 in penalities is equivalent to +2 Charm successes (for Solars). I think I prefer equating 2 penalty dice to 1 difficulty (round up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T02:36:04-07:00","id":1321365,"title":"","content":"Just a quick question. Sometimes a Charm specifies you need &quot;Magic&quot; to counter it's effects (I believe some Stealth or Detect lies charms), I guess Excellencies don't count as magic for the purpose of these. Like you can't lie to someone with the Solar Charm that detect lies with Excellencies alone, you'd need a &quot;Lie charm&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T04:00:55-07:00","id":1321373,"title":"","content":"Generally when it just specifies &quot;magic&quot; excellencies count. Essence is spent, ergo it's magic. Some charms are a bit more specific though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T05:24:02-07:00","id":1321379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321365#post1321365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a quick question. Sometimes a Charm specifies you need &quot;Magic&quot; to counter it's effects (I believe some Stealth or Detect lies charms), I guess Excellencies don't count as magic for the purpose of these. Like you can't lie to someone with the Solar Charm that detect lies with Excellencies alone, you'd need a &quot;Lie charm&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I play that Excellencies do not count. You need a specific charm. This is a house-rule.<br /> <br /> Word of Vance is that Excellencies count: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1207985#post1207985\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...85#post1207985</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-28-2019, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T05:50:02-07:00","id":1321380,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for your answers ! I don't know what to think about it, it seems to undermine a lot of the &quot;uniqueness&quot; of Charms","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T06:18:31-07:00","id":1321386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321380#post1321380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you both for your answers ! I don't know what to think about it, it seems to undermine a lot of the &quot;uniqueness&quot; of Charms</div> </div> </div> </div><s>In previous editions, Excellencies didn't count.</s> [Edit: Apparently they did.] In 3E Excellencies are pretty much all a Solar needs.<br /> <br /> I agree that letting them count is a blow to the uniqueness of charms. I think it also dilutes what an Excellency is: for me, Excellencies aren't about magic but rather they're an expression of how an Exalt performs a task really well (<i>excellently</i> if you will). For me, they're the peak expression of mundane ability dialled up to the max rather than a supernatural power <i>as such</i>. Thus, just as I wouldn't allow Athletics Excellency to replace Soaring Crane Leap, I wouldn't let an Excellency stand in for a specific charm to detect lies.<br /> <br /> But as I said, the Devs disagree and RAW the corebook defines Excellencies as charms and has no specific prohibition on their use to contest magic effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-28-2019, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T12:57:52-07:00","id":1321420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321386#post1321386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In previous editions, Excellencies didn't count. In 3E Excellencies are pretty much all a Solar needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>First Edition had no Excellencies, and die adders were normal Charms. In Second Edition, yeah, Excellencies counted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T13:06:06-07:00","id":1321424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321386#post1321386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In previous editions, Excellencies didn't count.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did. This is why so many DB charms were rubbish; you could stop them with just spending 2m to get +1 Parry or MDV or whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it also dilutes what an Excellency is: for me, Excellencies aren't about magic but rather they're an expression of how an Exalt performs a task really well (<i>excellently</i> if you will). For me, they're the peak expression of mundane ability dialled up to the max rather than a supernatural power <i>as such</i>. </div> </div> </div>I agree with you on the excellencies, but a lot of charms represent that too. Blazing Solar Bolt is a supernatural power, but stuff like Excellent Strike, Peony Blossom Strike, War Lion Stance, and Hungry Tiger Technique are just ways to make &quot;I'm an amazing swordsman&quot; more mechanically interesting than more dice. But they still just represent being an amazing swordsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T14:01:11-07:00","id":1321428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321424#post1321424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did. This is why so many DB charms were rubbish; you could stop them with just spending 2m to get +1 Parry or MDV or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Guess I've been houseruling that longer than I thought. Happily retracted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree with you on the excellencies, but a lot of charms represent that too. Blazing Solar Bolt is a supernatural power, but stuff like Excellent Strike, Peony Blossom Strike, War Lion Stance, and Hungry Tiger Technique are just ways to make &amp;quot;I'm an amazing swordsman&amp;quot; more mechanically interesting than more dice. But they still just represent being an amazing swordsman. </div> </div> </div>I kind of disagree.<br /> <br /> All the Solar charms are an extension of skill. Blazing Solar Bolt is the swordsman so skillful he can strike his foes from a distance, unleashing the shining glory of the sun. Excellencies, because they only add dice, don't do anything beyond doing what you do better.<br /> <br /> Excellent Strike is more like D&amp;D's True Strike. It flat out stops you botching, using magic to strike true and harden your attack against mystical defences. Peony Blossom Strike imbues you with such supernatural potency that you can attack twice as fast as any mortal swordsman could ever achieve. Likewise War Lion Stance reflective nature is much more than a mortal could achieve by flurrying. Hungry Tiger technique, I'll give you, is basically an Excellency for damage, but I still see it as using magic to rend your opponent apart in a way that a mortal just can't replicate.<br /> <br /> But Excellencies... a Solar swordsman with Dex 2 Melee 2 can use an Excellency to buy 4 more dice. A mortal swordsman can use XP to buy their stats up to 4 to get those dice. Excellencies are far closer to &quot;more of the same but better&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T01:14:03-07:00","id":1321477,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but when do you see a Solar swordsman with Dex 2 and Melee 2?<br /> That's not a Solar Swordsman, that's a Solar doctor whose player doesn't care about combat.<br /> (My Zenith had Dex 2, Brawl 1, as his character arc was supposed to be learning kung-fu because he was too bad at combat to defeat his nemesis.)<br /> <br /> Even a non-combat-focused character is more likely to be Dex 3, Melee 3, and 90% of Solar swordsmen will start with Dex 3+ and Melee 5.<br /> At which point excellencies are giving you supernatural skill beyond what any mortal can achieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-29-2019, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T02:04:16-07:00","id":1321480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321477#post1321477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but when do you see a Solar swordsman with Dex 2 and Melee 2?<br /> That's not a Solar Swordsman, that's a Solar doctor whose player doesn't care about combat.<br /> (My Zenith had Dex 2, Brawl 1, as his character arc was supposed to be learning kung-fu because he was too bad at combat to defeat his nemesis.)<br /> <br /> Even a non-combat-focused character is more likely to be Dex 3, Melee 3, and 90% of Solar swordsmen will start with Dex 3+ and Melee 5.<br /> At which point excellencies are giving you supernatural skill beyond what any mortal can achieve.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what can you do with it?<br /> <br /> With Dex 5, Athletics 5, a Spec in &quot;jumping&quot; and 10 Excellency dice, you can jump really well. But you can't leap to the top of a building in a single bound. With Dex 1, Athletics 2 and Monkey Leap Technique you CAN leap to the top of that building.<br /> <br /> With Excellent Strike, a Solar Swordswoman can never botch. It's not unlikely, it's impossible. With the Excellency, she's just better at sword fighting. And yes, she's better than any mortal can hope to be, but it's a linear progression of skill. It's N+1. She's not doubling her attacks per round, or breaking the turn order, or ignoring magical armor, or pulling a blade from nowhere. She's just doing what the mortal does... only better.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'm a 5/5/1 min-maxer all the way, but the 3E corebook makes clear that a Dex 2, Melee 2 character is capable with a sword. I don't write the books, I just play here.<br /> <br /> But, again, I don't disagree that Solar charms are dialled up expressions of skill. My point is only that Excellencies are the most basic expression of that, and that my preferred aesthetic is not for Excellencies to be <i>overtly</i> &quot;magical&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T02:30:41-07:00","id":1321485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, I'm a 5/5/1 min-maxer all the way, but the 3E corebook makes clear that a Dex 2, Melee 2 character is capable with a sword. I don't write the books, I just play here. </div> </div> </div>Hah, that's true*! Sometimes the way the books are written, I wonder if they've actually read the character gen system.<br /> (And I think you don't need to be a 5/5/1 min-maxer to see that getting a combat Ability to 5 for Solars is so trivially easy and useful that not doing so is basically a deliberate decision. All of my Solar and Dragonblood characters who haven't had a combat Ability at 5 are because I've said to myself &quot;I want a character who's bad at combat&quot;.<br /> Lunars are different of course. I'm finding that running a Lunar game, everyone's taken much more sensible spreads. Only one guy has a combat ability higher than 3, the Full Moon whose concept is &quot;guy with a giant axe made of his own walrus-tusk&quot;.<br /> But with Solars, everyone has a combat ability at 5 except for the character of the player who doesn't like combat.)<br /> <br /> *Though I mean, they are. I just wouldn't describe them as a Solar swordsman, is my point. They're of decent mortal skill with a sword; clearly this is their tertiary area, and they're amazing at something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321480#post1321480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, again, I don't disagree that Solar charms are dialled up expressions of skill. My point is only that Excellencies are the most basic expression of that, and that my preferred aesthetic is not for Excellencies to be <i>overtly</i> &quot;magical&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not arguing with that. It's just that John Morke was really keen on explaining that a lot of charms beyond exellencies aren't overtly magical (actually I think he went a bit overboard, Blazing Solar Bolt clearly is magical). And I think stuff like &quot;never totally screws up a strike&quot; aren't that overtly magical either. (A standing jump of 15 foot is pretty overt though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-29-2019, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T03:11:33-07:00","id":1321490,"title":"","content":"Blazing Solar Bolt is magical in the way that waterbending is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T03:14:04-07:00","id":1321491,"title":"","content":"No objection there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T03:33:40-07:00","id":1321494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321491#post1321491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No objection there.</div> </div> </div> </div>{narrowed eyes and Patti LuPone voice} Why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T03:53:31-07:00","id":1321495,"title":"","content":"Because, I assume, I agree with you?<br /> <br /> Waterbending is magic. But it's not like a DnD wizard who knows &quot;waterstrike (lvl1), watergrapple (lvl1), healing (lvl2)&quot;. It's the magical ability to manipulate water, which can be learnt to be used in different ways, but is still fundamentally the same power.<br /> <br /> A Solar swordsman doesn't know &quot;Blazing Solar Bolt&quot; like a spell, and when she uses it people won't be &quot;Wow, she just cast Blazing Solar Bolt!&quot;<br /> Rather, she's combined her incredible skill with a sword (not in of itself magical) with her magical Sun-powers in order to throw forth a blade made of magical blazing sun energy. Something very obviously magical, but not like a sorcerer casting Death of Obsidian Butterflies.<br /> <br /> (Is that not what you meant? I'm afraid I have no idea what a Patti LuPone voice sounds like so don't really understand that reference. Google tells me she's an American actress, but I don't recognise her. I'm not an expert on American actresses.)<br /> <br /> I think, tbh, it might have been better for charms to say they could be countered with &quot;Charms&quot; (and some note somewhere saying that Evocations and Spells count), rather than &quot;magic&quot;, as &quot;magic&quot; isn't really defined in Exalted (is an Elemental a magical creature so all its attacks are magic? Are excellencies magic when they just represent immense skill? Basically this whole debate). And there's that whole sidebar Morke wrote about charms not being spells, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Certainly, whenever I see &quot;this charm can be resisted by magic&quot; or &quot;effects enhanced by magic&quot; or whatever, I just assume they mean charms/spells/evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-29-2019, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T04:25:48-07:00","id":1321497,"title":"","content":"Cloooose enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T06:33:56-07:00","id":1321503,"title":"","content":"Cool. /10char","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T11:44:59-07:00","id":1321525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321477#post1321477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but when do you see a Solar swordsman with Dex 2 and Melee 2?<br /> That's not a Solar Swordsman, that's a Solar doctor whose player doesn't care about combat.<br /> (My Zenith had Dex 2, Brawl 1, as his character arc was supposed to be learning kung-fu because he was too bad at combat to defeat his nemesis.)<br /> <br /> Even a non-combat-focused character is more likely to be Dex 3, Melee 3, and 90% of Solar swordsmen will start with Dex 3+ and Melee 5.<br /> At which point excellencies are giving you supernatural skill beyond what any mortal can achieve.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Solar Dawn Caste Martial Artist - Dex 4 Melee 4, Martial Art (Single Point Void) 5 (plus 3 other Martial Arts 3+). Definitely Supernatural with Excellencies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But I am a Peace First kind of Dawn Caste, so... Maybe I am weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T13:45:49-07:00","id":1321537,"title":"","content":"You don't have Dex 5? Or a +1 specialty?<br /> <br /> Sounds like a pretty relaxed and non-optimised Dawn from what I've seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T14:12:10-07:00","id":1321542,"title":"","content":"I apologize for coming to the difficulties discussion late, but I ran into an interesting bit in the core book about difficulties greater than five on page 238. Granted, this is specifically relating to testing Lore pools, but there was a clear idea that, at least when it the core book was written, difficulty five was not the be all, end all most difficult test.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T14:18:45-07:00","id":1321543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321537#post1321537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have Dex 5? Or a +1 specialty?<br /> <br /> Sounds like a pretty relaxed and non-optimised Dawn from what I've seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do have a specialty - Martial Arts (Multiple Opponents)<br /> No Dex 5 (Str 3, Dex 4, Stam 4)<br /> He is a bit relaxed in some ways, to be sure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Many of my Favored Abilities fall outside of the Dawn Caste, and I have a lot of skills outside of Caste/Favored.<br /> No Thrown, Almost no Brawl, Archery not Caste or Favored, No War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-29-2019, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T15:09:29-07:00","id":1321546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inertial Frame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321542#post1321542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize for coming to the difficulties discussion late, but I ran into an interesting bit in the core book about difficulties greater than five on page 238. Granted, this is specifically relating to testing Lore pools, but there was a clear idea that, at least when it the core book was written, difficulty five was not the be all, end all most difficult test.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;a crucial fact that forwards the plot should be revealed at difficulty 1-4; at 5-7 difficulties should be reserved for challenges to the greatest minds and should be used to excite players to rise to the <br /> occasion,&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not a million miles off my position of having 5 as a soft-cap. 1-4 for normal heroics. 5+ for exceptional circumstances. Let's read on...<br /> <br /> &quot;while Lore 8-10+ challenges should be the proving <br /> grounds of Solar masters, riddles which unlock or reveal the greatest secrets of Creation\u2019s history.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that kinda blows my position out of the water doesn't it? More successes (trivial with a Solar Excellency) buys you a better result. If a 10 success Lore roll can unlock the greatest secret in Creation then why shouldn't a twenty success Awareness roll let you hear tectonic plates?<br /> <br /> (For more examples of difficulties above 5 in the corebook, you can see the Antagonists section (off the top of my head, the Tyrant Lizard has a Parry of 6). It's obviously not a hard-cap.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T16:01:34-07:00","id":1321549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321546#post1321546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;a crucial fact that forwards the plot should be revealed at difficulty 1-4; at 5-7 difficulties should be reserved for challenges to the greatest minds and should be used to excite players to rise to the<br /> occasion,&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not a million miles off my position of having 5 as a soft-cap. 1-4 for normal heroics. 5+ for exceptional circumstances. Let's read on...<br /> <br /> &quot;while Lore 8-10+ challenges should be the proving<br /> grounds of Solar masters, riddles which unlock or reveal the greatest secrets of Creation\u2019s history.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that kinda blows my position out of the water doesn't it? More successes (trivial with a Solar Excellency) buys you a better result. If a 10 success Lore roll can unlock the greatest secret in Creation then why shouldn't a twenty success Awareness roll let you hear tectonic plates?<br /> <br /> (For more examples of difficulties above 5 in the corebook, you can see the Antagonists section (off the top of my head, the Tyrant Lizard has a Parry of 6). It's obviously not a hard-cap.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Parry of 6 isn't that difficult... My Essence 2 Dawn Caste has a Parry of 6. *shrug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T19:32:37-07:00","id":1321569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321549#post1321549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Parry of 6 isn't that difficult... My Essence 2 Dawn Caste has a Parry of 6. *shrug*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But the average mortal soldier's parry dv is what, 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T00:05:37-07:00","id":1321582,"title":"","content":"Something like that, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T01:58:29-07:00","id":1321585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321549#post1321549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Parry of 6 isn't that difficult... My Essence 2 Dawn Caste has a Parry of 6. *shrug*</div> </div> </div> </div>5/5/1/Stunt + Medium Weapon &amp; Mounted gets you to, like, 9. And that's pretty trivial from character creation. But I don't think anyone was trying to argue that 5 is the highest difficulty in the game.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Conscripts are 2. Battle ready troops are 4.<br /> <br /> Parry 3 &quot;is the rating of bandits, militia, thugs, low-rent mercenaries, and Exalts who don\u2019t focus on martial prowess.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-30-2019, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T02:46:18-07:00","id":1321591,"title":"","content":"Sounds about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T03:20:19-07:00","id":1321593,"title":"","content":"To continue with some scaling questions :<br /> <br /> Suppose I have a charm that allows me to do some exceptionnal stuff (Like Monkey Leap Technique to jump, or Feather Foot Style to run on surfaces). How would you handle difficulties for achieving feats while using them ?<br /> <br /> For example : If I just Monkey Leap technique to jump from the balcony of a palace to another place, would you require a roll ? What if the palace is crumbling beneath my feet ? What if there is a lot of wind ? I'm having trouble balancing this because the feat in itself is supposed to be beyond what the difficulty system allows you to do.<br /> <br /> What about you are running with Feather Foot Style on some Wyld Maelstrom Quicksand, would there be a difficulty ? How would you handle it ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T05:27:32-07:00","id":1321598,"title":"","content":"Monkey Leap doesn't require a roll; that's kind of the point of it. I guess if you jump onto a crumbling building you might need to roll to keep your balance, but the jump itself requires no roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T06:13:36-07:00","id":1321600,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't make the PCs roll because they're not going to fail the roll. <br /> <br /> Monkey Leap Technique just works. Throwing a &quot;now roll a difficulty 2 athletics check to not fall down&quot; is going to be pretty insulting to the Solar who (at least) has the Excellency along with (probably) 10+ dice in their pool. Unless it's a prelude to something dramatic (like combat or a protracted escape scene) and I want to run down their mote pool, you're just slowing down the game by making the PCs roll checks that they're never going to fail.<br /> <br /> Embrace the awesome. Let them auto succeed with a good stunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-30-2019, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T06:25:42-07:00","id":1321602,"title":"","content":"I know the simple action enabled by the Charm requires no roll. But the situations the PCs are in is rarely &quot;in vacuum&quot;. What if there is a howl of wind that makes the jump more complicated ? Or traps, a rain of arrows, or the enrivonment is very tenebrous and the character can't see very well ? I'm not so sure in this kind of situations I should just let the player do it without any roll. Some of them resolve with a different subsystem (If there is fire in the path of the jump, it could be a Resistance check), but not every situation can be refered to these subsystems. Do you never encounter those ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T06:45:10-07:00","id":1321603,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... honestly, no, it hasn't come up in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T07:17:16-07:00","id":1321604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321585#post1321585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5/5/1/Stunt + Medium Weapon &amp; Mounted gets you to, like, 9. And that's pretty trivial from character creation. But I don't think anyone was trying to argue that 5 is the highest difficulty in the game.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Conscripts are 2. Battle ready troops are 4.<br /> <br /> Parry 3 &quot;is the rating of bandits, militia, thugs, low-rent mercenaries, and Exalts who don\u2019t focus on martial prowess.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome - Point Taken...<br /> I try not to look too deeply into adversary/opponents stats as I play, rather than GM. <br /> So... good to know. Thanks<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T07:25:32-07:00","id":1321606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321602#post1321602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the simple action enabled by the Charm requires no roll. But the situations the PCs are in is rarely &quot;in vacuum&quot;. What if there is a howl of wind that makes the jump more complicated ? Or traps, a rain of arrows, or the enrivonment is very tenebrous and the character can't see very well ? I'm not so sure in this kind of situations I should just let the player do it without any roll. Some of them resolve with a different subsystem (If there is fire in the path of the jump, it could be a Resistance check), but not every situation can be refered to these subsystems. Do you never encounter those ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never had a situation like this in my games, but I think I'd simply split the challenge into 2 rolls. If the Exalt is trying something ridiculously extreme like jumping a chasm that has an active tornado in the middle, then that's 2 rolls - 1 for the jump and 1 for navigating a tornado. The jump automatically succeeds because of Monkey Leap, and then you can make them roll whatever is appropriate for them to navigate a tornado, which might be a second athletics roll or might be something else depending on their stunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T09:34:22-07:00","id":1321609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321602#post1321602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you never encounter those ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what being ST is all about my man.<br /> <br /> But the system exists to facilitate the drama. You want to track resources and risk failure when bean counting and threat adds to the story. You don't want to slow play to a crawl by making characters make Difficulty 0 Intelligence + Resistance checks in order to remember to breathe.<br /> <br /> Look at the difficulty chart on page 185 and look at the dice pools your PCs are throwing down.<br /> <br /> If an unusal case comes up, then as ST you have to adjudicate what roll, or multiple rolls, are appropriate. There's nothing wrong with making a PC make a Dexterity + Athletics check as part of their Monkey Leap. But you need to ask yourself &quot;why are they rolling?&quot;<br /> <br /> The first two questions to ask are:<br /> <br /> Will rolling make a difference to the drama?<br /> If failure on the roll would make a difference, is it a desirable difference (from a dramatic point of view)?<br /> <br /> If the answer to both of those is &quot;yes&quot; then you set a difficulty and dicepool (looking at page 185 to get an idea of the difficulty and cooperating with the PC to set the dicepool to their stunt).<br /> <br /> If the answer to either question is &quot;no&quot; (and in my experience that's more often than not) then let them stunt their success and move the story on.<br /> <br /> In the examples you've given, my question is &quot;then what?&quot; Ok, I have to jump in the dark. That's going to be a difficulty 2 roll according to page 185. I only have 6 dice, so I'll add five from my Excellency. If I can then rest for 1 hour and get those motes back, then is it really worth tracking?<br /> <br /> Or I need to jump a chasm whilst being shot with arrows. If I fail, I fall to my death and the game stops for two hours as I roll up a new character because I thought Monkey Leap Technique would let me jump the chasm without rolling. Is that desirable? (It might be, if I'm derailing the game or we're playing high lethality stakes, or the players like a sense of danger and the ever present spectre of death. But I generally find it's better if you don't kill off the PCs with random save-or-dies.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-30-2019, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T10:03:33-07:00","id":1321613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321609#post1321609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what being ST is all about my man.<br /> <br /> But the system exists to facilitate the drama. You want to track resources and risk failure when bean counting and threat adds to the story. You don't want to slow play to a crawl by making characters make Difficulty 0 Intelligence + Resistance checks in order to remember to breathe.<br /> <br /> Look at the difficulty chart on page 185 and look at the dice pools your PCs are throwing down.<br /> <br /> If an unusal case comes up, then as ST you have to adjudicate what roll, or multiple rolls, are appropriate. There's nothing wrong with making a PC make a Dexterity + Athletics check as part of their Monkey Leap. But you need to ask yourself &quot;why are they rolling?&quot;<br /> <br /> The first two questions to ask are:<br /> <br /> Will rolling make a difference to the drama?<br /> If failure on the roll would make a difference, is it a desirable difference (from a dramatic point of view)?<br /> <br /> If the answer to both of those is &quot;yes&quot; then you set a difficulty and dicepool (looking. at page 185 to get an idea of the difficulty and cooperating with the PC to set the dicepool to their stunt).<br /> <br /> If the answer to either question is &quot;no&quot; (and in my experience that's more often than not) then let them stunt their success and move the story on.<br /> <br /> In the examples you've given, my question is &quot;then what&quot;. Ok, I have to jump in the dark. That's going to be a difficulty 2 roll according to page 185. I only have 6 dice, so I'll add five from my Excellency. If I can then rest for 1 hour and get those motes back, then is it really worth tracking?<br /> <br /> Or I need to jump a chasm whilst being shot with arrows. If I fail, I fall to my death and the game stops for two hours as I roll up a new character because I thought Monkey Leap Technique would let me jump the chasm without rolling. Is that desirable? (It might be, if I'm derailing the game or we're playing high lethality stakes, or the players like a sense of danger and the ever present spectre of death. But I generally find it's better if you don't kill off the PCs with random save-or-dies.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I overall agree with you, but I think many of the situation presented have narratives stakes, whether about ressources (&quot;Can you escape the town when everyone is looking for you and you took an arrow in the knee ?&quot;) or about drama (&quot;I can't let this sacred spear be swallowed by the Wyld Quicksand, we promised we would bring it back !&quot;). I just wanted to see what were suggestions about the topic &quot;How do you chose difficulty about an extraordinary feat allowed by a Charm, but that would still require a roll because there are circumstances&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T14:51:38-07:00","id":1321641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321613#post1321613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I overall agree with you, but I think many of the situation presented have narratives stakes, whether about ressources (&amp;quot;Can you escape the town when everyone is looking for you and you took an arrow in the knee ?&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> or about drama (&amp;quot;I can't let this sacred spear be swallowed by the Wyld Quicksand, we promised we would bring it back !&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I just wanted to see what were suggestions about the topic &amp;quot;How do you chose difficulty about an extraordinary feat allowed by a Charm, but that would still require a roll because there are circumstances&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Using page 185.<br /> <br /> Is it the standard fare for heroes? If so, difficulty 1. Not sure why you're rolling this, but hey, it could happen.<br /> <br /> Are there serious complications? The corebook suggests &quot;in the dead of night, without sufficient light, in the midst of a howling storm&quot; (and I read that as an &quot;or&quot; statement, not an &quot;and&quot; statement but YMMV) as difficulty 2.<br /> <br /> So if I want to Monkey Leap, normally I don't roll. But in tenbourus darkness or a howling storm I'd make a difficulty 2 roll.<br /> <br /> A task that would daunt heroes, jumping in pitch darkness as the building collapses into an eternal chasm? Difficulty 3.<br /> <br /> With significant duress? As above but in a howling storm with the Wyld Hunt at my heels, that's difficulty 4.<br /> <br /> Near impossible? The aforementioned jump is 30 feet straight up at the bearest peak of Monkey Leap Technique's reach, that's a 5.<br /> <br /> And, generally speaking, I wouldn't put the difficulty above 5. You could if you really felt you must, but if the complications are any worse than that then I'd say it wasn't possible without bringing in more supporting charms. If the drama absolutely demanded that the task be attempted, I'd usually cut the PCs some slack and keep it at 5. If there's an utterly compelling reason to make it harder (maybe one PC just made the difficulty 5 roll, but another is trying the same feat but with markedly worse circumstances) then you can set any difficulty you like. Make it difficulty 9001 if you like. I'd suggest +1 for each significant factor above difficulty 5, but you're going to want to look at the dots on the PCs sheets and listen to the stunts and justifications being put forth, and not be afraid to use ST fiat to just say &quot;yes and&quot; or &quot;no but&quot;.<br /> <br /> I straight up wouldn't allow a character to try to jump 30 feet straight up without a charm like Monkey Leap Technique -- without a specific charm, you're limited to ~8 feet, and I don't care how many successes the Excellency buys you. And, as previously belaboured, I wouldn't generally make the PCs roll to jump whether they had a charm like Monkey Leap Technique (which explicitly includes the line &quot;without having to roll&quot;) or not -- unless there's a decent chance that they might fail, and failure itself (rather than the threat of failure) would further the drama.<br /> <br /> (The threat of failure is what makes things interesting for the players. But if they fail when the plot demands they succeed, it's just a headache for the ST. Your narration can provide the threat of failure better than rolling buckets of dice can. Only gamble with what you can afford to lose.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T13:28:18-07:00","id":1321768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321641#post1321641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Using page 185.<br /> <br /> Is it the standard fare for heroes? If so, difficulty 1. Not sure why you're rolling this, but hey, it could happen.<br /> <br /> Are there serious complications? The corebook suggests &quot;in the dead of night, without sufficient light, in the midst of a howling storm&quot; (and I read that as an &quot;or&quot; statement, not an &quot;and&quot; statement but YMMV) as difficulty 2.<br /> <br /> So if I want to Monkey Leap, normally I don't roll. But in tenbourus darkness or a howling storm I'd make a difficulty 2 roll.<br /> <br /> A task that would daunt heroes, jumping in pitch darkness as the building collapses into an eternal chasm? Difficulty 3.<br /> <br /> With significant duress? As above but in a howling storm with the Wyld Hunt at my heels, that's difficulty 4.<br /> <br /> Near impossible? The aforementioned jump is 30 feet straight up at the bearest peak of Monkey Leap Technique's reach, that's a 5.<br /> <br /> And, generally speaking, I wouldn't put the difficulty above 5. You could if you really felt you must, but if the complications are any worse than that then I'd say it wasn't possible without bringing in more supporting charms. If the drama absolutely demanded that the task be attempted, I'd usually cut the PCs some slack and keep it at 5. If there's an utterly compelling reason to make it harder (maybe one PC just made the difficulty 5 roll, but another is trying the same feat but with markedly worse circumstances) then you can set any difficulty you like. Make it difficulty 9001 if you like. I'd suggest +1 for each significant factor above difficulty 5, but you're going to want to look at the dots on the PCs sheets and listen to the stunts and justifications being put forth, and not be afraid to use ST fiat to just say &quot;yes and&quot; or &quot;no but&quot;.<br /> <br /> I straight up wouldn't allow a character to try to jump 30 feet straight up without a charm like Monkey Leap Technique -- without a specific charm, you're limited to ~8 feet, and I don't care how many successes the Excellency buys you. And, as previously belaboured, I wouldn't generally make the PCs roll to jump whether they had a charm like Monkey Leap Technique (which explicitly includes the line &quot;without having to roll&quot;) or not -- unless there's a decent chance that they might fail, and failure itself (rather than the threat of failure) would further the drama.<br /> <br /> (The threat of failure is what makes things interesting for the players. But if they fail when the plot demands they succeed, it's just a headache for the ST. Your narration can provide the threat of failure better than rolling buckets of dice can. Only gamble with what you can afford to lose.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting you start the difficulties quite low. I'm rather used to start a bit more high because the actual feat is way beyong what heroes are able to do, but considering there is a Charm in play it might make more sense to start the difficulty lower.<br /> <br /> Yeah with all the discussion here about how you shouldn't let people do superhuman stuff without Charms I'm pretty convinced now, I wouldn't let someone do that without a Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T04:40:39-07:00","id":1321863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1321768#post1321768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's interesting you start the difficulties quite low. I'm rather used to start a bit more high because the actual feat is way beyong what heroes are able to do, but considering there is a Charm in play it might make more sense to start the difficulty lower.<br /> <br /> Yeah with all the discussion here about how you shouldn't let people do superhuman stuff without Charms I'm pretty convinced now, I wouldn't let someone do that without a Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation of the rules, is that Solar charms are an expression of a Solar's skills enhanced by Essence.<br /> <br /> Anyone (baring disability, injury etc.) can jump a couple of feet into the air. A Solar with Monkey Leap Technique has realised how to jump a couple of dozen feet. With Essence, jumping to the top of a twenty foot wall is no different to jumping to the top of a two foot step for a normal, non-magical human.<br /> <br /> It's less that magic makes the task &quot;easier&quot; than magic makes the impossible ordinary.<br /> <br /> Jumping a trivial distance doesn't normally need a roll. Monkey Leap Technique changes what your character considers a trivial distance.<br /> <br /> You wouldn't be wrong in interpreting it differently. You could say that jumping 8 feet into the air is a &quot;nearly impossible&quot; difficulty 5 feat. Jumping 30 feet into the air is therefore more difficult (difficulty 6), serious complications would make that difficulty 7 (and so forth in that fashion upto difficulty 10).<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with that approach. And with the size of Solar dicepools, a Solar acting &quot;in focus&quot; will be able to succeed at epic feats and be challenged by &quot;appropriate&quot; difficulties. It makes dice trick charms more useful.<br /> <br /> I do not favour this approach.<br /> <br /> Higher difficulties makes the game more swingy. It usually means Solars are useless outside their area of focus, which discourages the players from trying unusual, creative solutions to their problems. If you need 6 charms to jump effectively, then no-one without those charms is ever going to try jumping but someone with those charms will try to solve all their problems with jumping. Failing the wrong roll can easily derail the game. And I don't think it reconciles with the fluff -- discounting DB fiction, how often to the signiture characters ever fail a straight difficulty roll?<br /> <br /> Attribute 5 and Ability 5 makes you the best in Creation. That should mean something. If you're still failing half your rolls because your feats are all difficulty 10+ then it feels cheap (and why would you ever take 2 or 3 dice in an Ability if you know you need to consistently hit difficulty 10+).<br /> <br /> Keeping a soft-cap of 5, keeps difficulties in line with the NPC quick stats. If it's difficulty 10 to jump to the top of the tower, but the guards only have a Resolve of 3, then I'd never climb anywhere -- I'd convince the guards to not only let me in but to carry me up.<br /> <br /> I'd be interested in how other people interpret it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-03-2019, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T04:39:36-07:00","id":1322010,"title":"","content":"You're making a lot of sense there, John.<br /> <br /> I for one think there's something interesting in your idea of introducing the odd roll with an appropriate difficulty even to a task that a Charm might otherwise make absolute when it seems to make sense. The increased jumping distance of a Solar Athletics Charm might readily cross a lot of gaps, but in the event where low light, heavy rain and battering wind might knock them off course or make them unable to properly aim themselves, it certainly seems as though there should be something to model the added complications.<br /> <br /> Doing so in the manner of the Charm making the success absolute in all circumstances strikes me as unsatisfying, and significantly curtailing a lot of dramatic situations and potential applications for the powers of enemies in opposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T06:17:19-07:00","id":1322016,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree with your general point John.<br /> <br /> There might be times when other people's magic makes things higher difficulty (attacking a Solar whose magic makes his Parry 8), but for 99% of anything else, I'd say difficulty 5 is going to be the max.<br /> (I can't think of any rolls I've set at difficulty 5 beyond that... maybe once or twice a difficulty 6 Lore or Occult roll to know some extremely obscure First Age lore? Once or twice in 10 years.)<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want a hard cap of 5, there might be some occasions, but a soft cap seems fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for doing a Monkey Leap while in the middle of a tornado, etc... I think if there was a roll, it should probably be lower than if you didn't use Monkey Leap. But rolling because you're doing it through a tornado seems fine. Maybe Strength+Athletics difficulty 3 or something.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T09:35:45-07:00","id":1322044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1322010#post1322010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one think there's something interesting in your idea of introducing the odd roll with an appropriate difficulty even to a task that a Charm might otherwise make absolute when it seems to make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Chausse's idea, I'm just helping to model it from my own experience and what guidance is in the books.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, I'm against rolling. Let the charm auto-succeed as writen and narrate any complications that seem logical. But if rolling adds to the drama, this is the system I'd use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1319165-trying-to-get-a-sense-of-scale-with-exalted?p=1322016#post1322016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There might be times when other people's magic makes things higher difficulty (attacking a Solar whose magic makes his Parry 8)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh definitely. That's the point of the heroic challenge. It should be more difficult to deal a telling blow to an epic hero who is renowned for her magical skill with her enchanted blade than it should be against a mortal swordsman. Beating Mercury in a footrace should not be as easy as beating Beowulf. There has to be scope for difficulties to go above five. It just should serve the drama and not turn into Deathknight of the week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-03-2019, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T21:40:31-07:00","id":1322153,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if performing monkey leap in a tornado would require a roll, would it? Or like on an icy slick frozen lake? You'd have to roll for balance unless you also had graceful crane I suppose but otherwise the charm lets you jump, so you jump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}